AD  - Vishnu Institute of Technology Bhimavaram, Bhimavaram, India
AD  - JNTUA College of Engineering, Kalikiri, Kalikiri, India
AB  - Currently, big data analysis has emerged as a significant research area. Big data security protects Cloud applications and monitors very sensitive data for assisting Cloud platforms. However, ensuring the security of big data remains a challenge, limiting organizations’ adoption of cloud services. In this article, a new model namely Adam One-to-One Based Optimizer for key generation (AOOBO_Keygen) is presented for secure Authentication and Access Control (AAC) in a cloud-enabled Big Data Environment. Firstly, the initialization of public key and security parameters are done. Next, the registration with trusted authority by the data user, data owner, and cloud server are done. Later, the data preservation is done using several operators and keys. After that, a novel optimization algorithm such as AOOBO_Keygen is utilized to generate the key, which is devised by combining the Adam optimizer and One-to-One Based Optimizer (OOBO). Then, the user is requested to log in. Further, the user's authenticity is validated with the key. Finally, the user sends a request to the trusted authority to access the data. Moreover, the AOOBO_Keygen is assessed for its effectiveness, and the least memory usage, computational cost, conditional privacy, and latency of 38.400 MB, 47.340, 92.842, and 3.178 s. are attained. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
