AB  - This work reports the evaluation of dicloxacillin (C<inf>19</inf>H<inf>16</inf>C<inf>12</inf>N<inf>3</inf>NaO<inf>5</inf>S⋅H<inf>2</inf>O) as a corrosion inhibitor for API 5L X65 steel in acidic media employing electrochemical impedance spectroscopy (EIS) and potentiodynamic polarization curves (PDP). Efficiency increases with concentration, with a maximum value of 76% according to EIS and 77% according to PDP at 100 ppm. Adsorption thermodynamics were studied by fitting EIS experimental data to adsorption isotherms revealing that dicloxacillin follows a mixed adsorption process with ΔG<inf>ads</inf> of −36.69 kJ mol−1. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
