AD  - Narasaraopeta Engineering College, Narasaraopet, India
AB  - In the contemporary age of cloud computing, a vast array of resources in the type of services is provided to the cloud clients upon demand to increase process output effectiveness. Due to cloud environments’ security concerns, consumers have lost the ability to regulate their private information. Although a lot of privacy-based solutions are expanding in scope and feature, customers’ security problems remain to be fully resolved. Nevertheless, a number safety measures, such as multifactor authorization, firewall defense, and image processing-based input identity, are insufficient to secure user private data. The suggested method, known as fuzzy oriented statistical process control (FSPC), will specifically carry out the duty of guaranteeing accessibility credentials and their matching authenticity aspects in addition to customer service level data. Measurement validation of data and information about attributes authentication is the two main activities that will complete the assessment of utilizes validity as well as safe data access. By creating membership functions, these procedures will actually be carried out the safety structure, and the results are recreated using the green cloud simulation tool. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
