AB  - Users surrender direct manipulate over their personal statistics after they pass it to cloud settings, which increases worries approximately feasible protection lapses and statistics leaks. Because cloud infrastructure is so complicated, it is able to be hard to preserve strict protection without compromising gadget overall performance. Because sturdy statistics safety and gadget overall performance need to be balanced, traditional protection strategies often fail to satisfy those demands. In order to cope with this, we endorse a version this is pushed through a tradeoff planner and assesses and optimizes protection methods according with the particular necessities and boundaries of cloud environments. The tradeoff planner unearths the exceptional protection configurations that strike a compromise among chance control and operational performance through methodically comparing variables like statistics sensitivity, person get right of entry to levels, and gadget overall performance. In order to save you undesirable get right of entry to even as keeping seamless gadget operation, this adaptive answer allows the dynamic change of protection protocols in reaction to converting threats and overall performance necessities. Experimental verification indicates that the planner is green at defensive statistics privateness even as having no impact on gadget overall performance as a whole. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
