AD  - Priyadarshani Bhagwati College of Engineering, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Nagpur, India
AD  - Priyadarshini College of Engineering, Nagpur, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Nagpur, India
AB  - Attribute-Based Encryption (ABE) is beneficial for fine-grained access control, especially in cloud computing. Hierarchical Ciphertext Policy Attribute-Based Encryption (HCP ABE) is an improvement over CP-ABE, as it features a multi-tiered key delegation structure that enhances both scalability and security. This leaves a few challenges, such as dynamic policy changes, user revocation, and the overhead cost it incurs. The paper deals with a comparative study of the CP-ABE and HCP-ABE in efficiency, scalability, policy flexibility, and security mechanisms. It gives a more modern take on dynamic policy management with real-time updates with minimal overhead. User revocation is considered in terms of attributes and key based approaches, with a measure of the costs against security and computational performance. The paper makes cases for HCP-ABE, which shows the advantages of efficient key distribution, fine-grained access control, as well as automated unauthorized access reduction. It creates a platform for applications that are HCP-ABE with blockchain and decentralized identity management at an increased level of trust and transparency. However, there are still high computational costs and quantum security issues. Future work is on the optimization of encryption schemes with post-quantum cryptographic approaches for large instance applications. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
