TI  - CloudShare: A Passwordless Cloud-Based File Storage and Sharing Framework
PY  - 2025
DO  - 10.1109/ICOCT64433.2025.11118777
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-105016314639&doi=10.1109%2FICOCT64433.2025.11118777&partnerID=40&md5=628d1230f8f03766989b70c2edc265c7
AD  - Amrita Vishwa Vidyapeetham University, Bangalore, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Bengaluru, India
AB  - Cloud-based file storage and sharing systems are widely used for collaborative work, data accessibility, and secure information dissemination. Traditional solutions often rely on password-based authentication, which introduces vulnerabilities such as credential theft, reuse attacks, and usability challenges. This paper presents CloudShare, a passwordless cloud-based file storage and sharing framework that enhances both security and user experience. CloudShare utilizes a challenge-response authentication protocol with asymmetric cryptography, eliminating the need for passwords while maintaining strong identity assurance. Users can upload, download, and securely share files with others, while file access is enforced through cryptographic ownership and explicit sharing permissions. The framework also introduces time-based access control mechanisms, enabling users to restrict file availability to specific time windows. The system is implemented using a web-based frontend and serverless backend architecture, offering scalability, ease of use, and end-to-end file confidentiality. CloudShare provides a practical and more secure alternative to traditional file sharing systems, particularly for environments where passwordless, controlled, and verifiable access is essential. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
