AD  - Galgotias University, School of Computing Science and Engineering, Greater Noida, India
AB  - Cloud Cloud Computing is one of the most emerging technologies and many industries, as well as consumers, are significantly shifting towards cloud servers for storing their data. However, there are a few security issues are there in the cloud and this requires little development to increase the efficiency and reliability of the Cloud. There are many sources such as address resolution protocol (ARP), IP spoofing, Botnets, Distributed Denial of Service attack (DDoS) etc where in different attacks can originate and plays a huge role in destroying sensitive data. It will completely describe how we can protect our crucial data by minimizing the risk and threats associated with this. Nowadays cloud computing is used by many organizations for storing their data, and the source of data comes from various places and a few weak data may corrupt other data. There is a need to understand the security issues and their challenges in this area. Security issues are one of the major concerns which have been affecting the growth of cloud technologies. In this paper, a comparative analysis is presented related to security and privacy techniques in cloud computing. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
