AB  - A revolutionary new paradigm in cloud security has emerged through the integration of Artificial Intelligence (AI), Zero Trust Architecture (ZTA), and predictive analytics. This integrated strategy makes use of AI to detect and respond to threats in real-time in cloud environment. In addition, predictive analytics reveal potential flaws and dangers that could be exploited. To make it resistant to quantum decryption attacks, it uses post-quantum cryptographic (PQC) methods, and to speed up threat identification and adaptive policy enforcement, it employs quantum machine learning (QML). In order to build a next-generation cloud security model with quantum-resistant qualities, this research presents a new framework that combines AI capabilities with Zero Trust Architecture (ZTA) principles with Frequent Pattern Analysis (AI-ZTA-FPA). The system is able to forecast possible security breaches, recognize unusual activities, and dynamically alter access controls across remote cloud environments by utilizing supervised and unsupervised AI techniques. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
