AD  - Karpagam College of Engineering, Department of EEE, Coimbatore, India
AB  - Accurate speech transcription fulfills essential functions like accessibility and documentation and automated communication while background noises cause major obstacles to the accuracy rate. The research presents a speech-to-text system which combines edge computing with deep learning and cloud services to deliver better transcription results. An edge device based on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B handles the process of audio capture and pre-processing. The noise reduction capabilities of the RNN model use LSTM units for dynamic disturbance filtering to enhance speech clarity. The service Amazon Transcribe receives refined audio data which it uses to generate text with high accuracy through its cloud-based speech recognition capabilities. AWS S3 provides secure high-scale storage that depends on encryption features alongside versioning and access authorization tools. A MERN stack-based dashboard that combines MongoDB, Express.js, React.js, Node.js lets users conduct interactive searches and filtration operations and transcription administration through an interface. Traditional noise suppression techniques break down when sound environments change but the adaptive RNN model both learns new information and enhances itself thus leading to better speech recognition accuracy in multiple real-life situations. This system functions best for lecture recording as well as corporate meeting recordings and accessibility tool applications and automatic documentation system processing. This study achieves a versatile high-sensitivity and cost-optimized transcription system through its real-time edge computing tech and AI noise filtration systems and scalable cloud platform design. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
