AD  - Sathyabama Institute of Science and Technology, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Chennai, India
AB  - The Event Organization System (EOS) is an advanced platform designed to streamline the planning, execution, and analysis of events. By leveraging cutting-edge technologies such as cloud computing, artificial intelligence (AI), blockchain, and the Internet of Things (IoT), the system automates tasks like scheduling, attendee communication, ticketing, and post-event analytics. The platform ensures scalability, accessibility, and enhanced security through cloud-based infrastructure and blockchain-powered ticketing and access control. IoT sensors provide real-time monitoring, while AI-driven analytics enable personalized experiences and actionable insights. The mobile-first design ensures a user-friendly interface, offering organizers and participants an intuitive experience. The system reduces manual effort, improves efficiency, and enhances the overall success of events. Tested and verified, the EOS meets all organizational requirements, providing a centralized, secure database and robust tools to revolutionize event management. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
