AD  - S.J.C. Institute of Technology, Dept. of Ise, Chikkaballapur, India
AB  - Cloud computing become an essential tool for various sectors, Because of its scalable, on- demand nature, it is suitable for use by industry, academia, and the government. However, it confronts major security concerns, notably with regard to data confidentiality, integrity, and access control. This study provides a detailed overview of cloud security concerns and investigates alternative machine learning-based ways for minimizing these risks. We look at a variety of strategies intended to improve cloud security, including probabilistic models, techniques for deep learning, and encryption methods. These techniques address concerns like as DDoS assaults, virus detection, and unauthorized access to data. Despite these developments, security problems remain, particularly in regards to implementation difficulty and adaptability. The consideration concludes with a discussion of future developments and the need for more robust, real-world safety systems groups to battle underused risks in cloud platforms to address emerging threats in cloud environments. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
