AD  - Inner Mongolia University of Science and Technology, School of Information Engineering, Baotou, China
AB  - In view of the problems existing in the current communication system, such as the diversity of standards, the inability to uniformly plan resources, low utilization, and poor communication quality, this paper proposes a multi-standard communication fusion system based on cloud computing technology. First, the system architecture is designed, including key components such as user management module, communication resource management module, multi-standard fusion module, and cloud computing platform. The user management module handles core functions such as user registration, login, and identity authentication to ensure that only legitimate users can access system resources. The communication resource management module allocates and adjusts various communication resources. The multi-standard fusion module is responsible for achieving fusion and interoperability between different communication standards. The cloud computing platform, as the supporting environment of the system, provides infrastructure and operating environment. In order to ensure the security and reliability of the system, this paper also adopts data encryption, access control, fault detection and recovery, etc. to prevent illegal access and attacks. The resource utilization of the cloud computing system can maintain a high level under different test conditions, with a maximum value of 84.8%, while the maximum resource utilization of the traditional system is 73.5%. In addition, the average bit error rate of the cloud computing system is 0.3135%, which is lower than the 0.5045% of the traditional system, showing the advantages of cloud computing technology in improving communication quality and reliability. This paper provides an effective solution to cope with the diverse challenges in communication systems and provides a new direction for the development of future communication systems. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
