AD  - Sathyabama Institute of Science and Technology, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Chennai, India
AB  - This project is aimed at addressing increasing security issues in cloud environments through the use of soft computing methods. It performs real-time detection and classification of security incidents through dynamic analysis of network traffic, user activity logs, and other public data sources. The system uses adaptive learning models that are constantly updated to identify new threats while reducing false alarms and providing means for automated responses. The architecture proposed consistently monitors and classifies security events as per risk levels and industry best practices, paving the way for proactive defense strategies. An optimized feedback loop enables the system to improve its performance according to past security events, improving its resistance to new-generation cyber threats. By incorporating robust encryption and access control mechanisms, the framework protects cloud resources without impacting performance or availability. This proactive solution enhances organizational cybersecurity by neutralizing threats, enhancing structural protections, and averting unauthorized access to confidential information. The solution is a notable innovation in cloud security that meets the dynamic challenges of a rapidly interconnected digital environment. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
