AB  - Any hospital management system must include health records. However, because clinical institutions are sending largely health data, they have no way to control or maintain their own medical records. Electronic health records, or EHRs, are a systematic to collect electronic health information about specific individuals' patients or populations. Cloud computing is becoming an important aspect of the health operation. In this paper, we suggest a scalable and safe cloud-based system for managing electronic health records. The architecture enables patients and other medical stakeholders in healthcare institutions to access the EHR system through universal healthcare service providers using a range of devices in a contextual setting. This study examines the effectiveness of the cloud-based EHR system by taking into account important elements such as user access control, data integrity, and the confidentiality and availability of medical records. The suggested approach effectively addresses security issues, including the compromise of private health information. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
