AD  - Galgotias University, Greater Noida, India
AB  - Cloud computing has revolutionized the way organizations store, process, and manage data. However, the increasing reliance on cloud services raises significant security concerns. This paper explores the critical challenges in cloud security, including data breaches, compliance issues, and vulnerabilities in shared infrastructure. It also examines current strategies employed to mitigate these risks, such as encryption, access control, and multi-factor authentication. Furthermore, the paper highlights emerging trends and technologies in cloud security, including AI-driven security solutions and the implementation of zero-trust architectures. By understanding the landscape of cloud security, organizations can better protect their data and maintain trust with their stakeholders. As more companies migrate their activities to the cloud, robust security measures have become top priority. This research is exploring the main challenges of cloud security and focusing on software development approaches, multi-layered encryption, IAM, and threat detection using artificial intelligence and machine learning. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
