AB  - With increasing reliance on cloud computing for data storage, processing, and service delivery, unprecedented convenience and efficiency have been brought. However, challenges in terms of data security and network security are enormous. This book chapter deals with the foundational principles, emerging threats, and innovative solutions associated with securing data and networks in cloud environments. It explores encryption techniques, access control mechanisms, and intrusion detection systems designed to be suitable for cloud ecosystems. In addition, it explores methods of reducing Distributed Denial of Service attacks and protecting against data breaches. It also addresses the issue of compliance with data protection regulations as well as the role of artificial intelligence and machine learning in cloud security. By presenting case studies and future trends, this chapter provides a broad overview of the emergent landscape of cloud security and practical insights for researchers and practitioners. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
