AD  - Karpagam Academy of Higher Education, Head Of the Department, Coimbatore, India
AD  - Karpagam Academy of Higher Education, Department of Computer Science, Coimbatore, India
AB  - Cloud computing is emerging as a predominant interactive framework for accessing users' data stored remotely on an Internet cloud server. Cloud services provide substantial benefits, allowing the customers to utilize on-demand apps irrespective of their local infrastructure limitations. During data access, several users are collaborated. It makes data sharing essential for realizing productive advantages. This project provides a collaborative governance paradigm for data sharing to address the previously noted privacy issues in cloud storage. The project achieves shared access authority via a method for matching anonymous access requests, addressing security and privacy concerns. Data access is granted only with the approval from cloud infrastructure and file owner. The shared access authority obtains and distributes the data solicited by users. This project enhancement entails a time-server access mechanism for secure data retrieval in the cloud, with files encrypted before storage. The encryption process utilizes symmetric key cryptography. The user secures authorization from a primary server to access the file directory or locate a specific file. The primary server recognizes the user's request and permits to select a file from the list. Then, the file owner receives an access request and upon acceptance, grants the secret key to the requesting user. It allows in viewing and downloading the material. If the user fails to submit a request within seconds, the primary server redirect to the mainpage. If the users need access to the file list again, the users have to obtain authorization from the primary server. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
