AD  - Manipal University Jaipur, Department of Information Technology, Jaipur, India
AB  - Digital life involves storing, processing, and managing data. Cyber security and cloud computing are the most important porticos of today’s digital life. Cybersecurity in cloud platforms is a critical concern since the increasing proliferation and reliance on cloud-based services have introduced new security challenges. This chapter investigates the security landscape of major cloud platforms, examining a few key areas such as identity and access management (IAM), encryption and key management systems, threat detection and prevention mechanisms, vulnerability management tools, and cloud security posture management (CSPM) tools. The study analyzes how IAM practices establish strong user authentication and authorization protocols, thwarting unauthorized access to profound data. It investigates the encryption techniques employed, including key generation, management, and distribution, to safeguard data at rest and in transit. Additionally, the chapter explores the effectiveness of threat detection and prevention measures and vulnerability management tools in mitigating cyber threats within cloud environments. Finally, the chapter examines the role of CSPM tools in providing an all-inclusive view of an organization’s cloud security posture, enabling proactive risk management and continuous improvement. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
