AD  - Beijing University of Posts and Telecommunications, Beijing, China
AD  - Hulu, LLC, Santa Monica, United States
AB  - The rapid expansion of the cloud computing industry has underscored the critical importance of data security. One of the typical realms is the management of subscription-based software licenses. Traditional license management models, which store licenses in plaintext on the client side, are vulnerable to tampering, unauthorized sharing, and local time manipulation. These vulnerabilities compromise the integrity and profitability of cloud service providers. This paper proposes a mechanism to address these issues, introducing the concepts of an Authorization Service and the Optimized License Union and Short-Lived Effectiveness. The proposed new mechanism is effective in securing licenses with minimal performance overhead, providing a robust solution for license management in cloud computing environments. Future work will aim to refine this mechanism further and explore additional security measures. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
