AB  - The logistics industry is rapidly transforming, driven by emerging technologies and evolving cybersecurity threats. These threats have also affected the industries financially on one side but also fined some of the most reputed industries due to poor quality supplied to the customers. Many cybersecurity threats have also been reported. However, due to the usage of cloud services, many more threats have been opened to this industry. Therefore, this study explores the complex relationship between logistics and cybersecurity, highlighting the industry's challenges and opportunities. The adoption of technologies like the Internet of Things (IoT), cloud computing, and artificial intelligence offers new possibilities for efficiency and visibility, but also introduces cybersecurity vulnerabilities that must be addressed. From securing supply chains to implementing advanced encryption and access control, logistics companies are navigating a dynamic landscape that demands proactive cybersecurity measures. Furthermore, this study underscores the importance of staying informed about emerging threats and trends while adopting innovative solutions to protect data, operations, and customer trust in an interconnected world. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
