AB  - With the widespread adoption of cloud storage and file systems, security concerns have become paramount. This paper presents an advanced investigation into the security challenges encountered in cloud storage and file systems. We explore the vulnerabilities and threats that these systems face, ranging from unauthorized access to data breaches and insider attacks. Additionally, we examine the evolving landscape of security solutions, including encryption techniques, access control mechanisms, and intrusion detection systems. Through a comprehensive review of existing literature and case studies, we identify emerging trends and best practices for mitigating security risks in cloud storage and file systems. Our analysis provides valuable insights for researchers, practitioners, and organizations seeking to enhance the security posture of their cloud-based infrastructure. Cloud storage and file systems have revolutionized data management, offering scalability, flexibility, and accessibility. However, alongside their benefits, they present formidable security challenges. This paper conducts an advanced investigation into the security landscape of cloud storage and file systems, aiming to interpret key challenges and propose effective solutions. Through a thorough examination of prevalent security threats, including unauthorized access, data breaches, and insider attacks, this study identifies vulnerabilities inherent in cloud environments. Moreover, it scrutinizes emerging security technologies such as encryption, access control mechanisms, and intrusion detection systems, assessing their efficacy in mitigating risks. By synthesizing insights from existing literature and real-world case studies, this investigation provides valuable guidance for enhancing the security posture of cloud-based infrastructure. Ultimately, this paper contributes to the ongoing discourse on cloud security by offering nuanced analyses and actionable recommendations to researchers, practitioners, and stakeholders alike. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
