AD  - University of Žilina, Faculty of Management Science and Informatics, Zilina, Slovakia
AB  - The development of a universal administration module for the 3DBody Anatomical Atlas is aimed at creating a flexible and scalable solution for managing users and roles within the 3DBody platform. The module offers functionalities such as user account creation, role assignment, and permission management, with a focus on securing access using JWT -based authentication. Built using modern technologies including Angular for the frontend,. NET for the backend, and PostgreSQL for data storage, the module is designed for easy integration across web, desktop, and mobile platforms. The API-driven architecture ensures that new features can be introduced without disrupting existing functionality. Administration module was designed to be universal and adaptable, and it is suitable to implement in various systems, not just 3DBody platform. Through the adoption of unit testing, static code analysis, CI/CD pipelines, and comprehensive API documentation, the administration module is well-positioned for continued development, supporting the evolving needs of the 3DBody platform and its users. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
