AB  - Cloud computing has revolutionized the way organizations manage and utilize computing resources, offering flexibility, scalability, and cost-effectiveness. The move to cloud settings has, however, also raised new security concerns that need to be taken into consideration. This research paper assesses the security risks that Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS) cloud settings now face and investigates possible optimisation techniques to strengthen security posture. This paper explores a number of cloud security topics, such as network security, identity and access control, data protection, and compliance issues. It also examines at how dynamic communication protocols help strengthen security and reduce vulnerabilities. This paper seeks to offer useful insights and recommendations for organisations looking to optimise their IaaS security and maximise the advantages of cloud computing while minimising risks. It does this by analysing current industry trends, best practices, and cutting-edge technology. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
