AD  - University of Mumbai, Mumbai, India
AD  - University of Mumbai, Department of Computer Engineering, Mumbai, India
AB  - The concept of data auditing has been developed due to the increasing concern about the safety of data stored in the cloud which can be attacked externally or modified without authorization. The main objective of this work is to involves assessing data integrity through a Third-Party Auditor (TPA). The audit request triggers an Anomaly Detection module which analyzes patterns to identify any unusual or malicious behavior. This study focuses on identifying and mitigating malicious TPAs in cloud-based data storage using privacy-preserving public auditing. Simulation results carried out using Python tool. The improvement enables TPA to handle multiple authorization audits concurrently thus enhancing the overall efficiency of the auditing system. The suggested system is both secure and efficient, according to a thorough evaluation of its performance and security. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
