AB  - In the scene of distributed computing, guaranteeing powerful information security stays vital. This paper digs into an essential progress from customary encryption techniques, including AES, DES, RC6, and LSB steganography, towards the reconciliation of multi-party encryption for strengthened information security in cloud conditions. The shift means to address impediments in existing safety efforts, especially in working with secure document dividing between assorted clients. This study frames the strategy, underlining the precise course of carrying out multi-party encryption while featuring its expected effect on framework proficiency, security, and ease of use. Through exact examination and exhaustive assessment, this exploration attempts to feature the adequacy of the progress, at last upgrading information trustworthiness and access control in cloud-based document sharing practices. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
