AB  - Protecting the confidentiality of patient's personal health information as it is sent and kept in the cloud is of the utmost importance due to the increasing number of telehealth services. This research provides a new healthcare data security approach using cloud computing and the Isolation Forest method. To identify important challenges and provide a novel technique, a thorough literature study on telehealth security, privacy issues, and cloud-based solutions. It uses the Isolation Forest method for anomaly detection in combination with encryption and access restriction systems to identify intrusion attempts. It uses simulated telehealth data in trials to test the system's work. Findings show substantial gains in privacy and data security with computational burden. Healthcare practitioners and legislators will find results useful in their pursuit of solutions to the problem of securing patients' private health information throughout the rise of telemedicine. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
