AD  - Bennett University, School of Computer Science Engineering and Technology, Greater Noida, India
AB  - The effective transmission and sampling of clinical images are important research areas in computer science, particularly in the healthcare industry. Methods such as personal area networking and body area networking are valuable for medical monitoring systems used in remote surgical guidance and early emergency detection. However, due to the sensitive nature of medical images, strong privacy protection and secure data aggregation/compression techniques are needed. In this study, we use compressive sensing theory to address these challenges with a novel approach. Our technique reduces the size of medical photos by 10 %, while maintaining strong secrecy through the use of additive homomorphic encryption. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
