AB  - The supervision of data storage systems that are centered on the cloud has become more important for both the academic and industrial communities. Service providers must ensure the secure and reliable exchange of data while maintaining user privacy and data confidentiality on a network that is easily accessible. While encryption is commonly used to protect sensitive data, relying exclusively on AES for data encryption is inadequate for addressing data management challenges. Implementing a strong access control mechanism for data exchange requests is crucial to prevent Economic Denial of Sustainability (EDoS) attacks and guarantee continuous service access for users. This article explores access control in cloud-based storage, focusing on creating a method to oversee data access requests while maintaining security and efficiency. This paper advocates two distinct access control systems, each designed for a specific environment, and provides a comprehensive analysis of their security and experimental aspects. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
