AD  - Karunya Institute of Technology and Sciences, Department, Coimbatore, India
AB  - For the purpose of enhancing cloud security, MA-AMFES is an all-encompassing system that employs robust encryption techniques and a multi-authority authentication mechanism. It is possible to improve the system's resistance against attempts to acquire unauthorized access by distributing authentication responsibilities among a large number of authorities. This allows for the reduction of the effect of single points of failure. By using encryption, MA-AMFES ensures that both the transfer of data and its storage in the cloud are protected from unauthorized access. Administrators are able to fulfill the specific security requirements of their businesses when they have the capability to set granular access controls over their systems. The MA-AMFES system is able to seamlessly integrate into a variety of cloud infrastructures, which allows it to retain optimal performance. The system is both scalable and interoperable. MA-AMFES offers a trustworthy solution for securing sensitive information with fault tolerance mechanisms that ensure sustained operation and data integrity. This solution is provided in light of the ongoing evolution of cloud computing. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
