AD  - Nanning University, Nanning, China
AD  - NO.6 Vocational Technical School of Nanning, Nanning, China
AB  - This study addresses the development and the evaluation of an adaptive security policy model for intelligent financial systems. The primary goal is to establish a dynamic and resilient security framework that can adapt to evolving threats and changing conditions in real time. The study reviewed various software system security algorithms, focusing on methods such as ordered matrix matching, zero watermarking, and hybrid automated security frameworks. The proposed methodology emphasizes access control, dynamic behavior detection, and the honey net system for security monitoring. The implementation of the policy management framework and intrusion detection system (IDS) in ERP systems enhances real-time monitoring, feature-based and behavior-based detection, log analysis, and multi-level protection. Experiments were conducted on the Huawei TMSS platform using automated test scripts to evaluate the cloud-based data management and intrusion detection capabilities. The results demonstrate accurate data storage, effective multi-site synchronization, timely alerts, comprehensive analysis reports, and system stability under heavy load conditions, indicating the robust functionality and reliability of the proposed security model. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
