AB  - In a distributed system environment, cloud computing describes a new technology that lets customers pay for the services they utilize as needed. Cloud service companies that prioritize maximum security supply a plethora of resources, including Infrastructure, Software, Platform, and Database. The literature has a wealth of security measures, such as Service Level Agreements (SLAs), access control rules, and cryptographic methods. This work implements a novel compound data encryption technique called Data Security in Cloud Computing using Maritime Search and Rescue Algorithm (DSCC-MSRA). It integrates the advantages of an enhanced cypher block chaining algorithm having logical substitution with an optimization algorithm called MSRA for key generation. This encryption method uses a different algorithm for generating keys. This method is optimized to a reasonable degree by running it through a variety of security as well as statistical analyses. This ground-breaking method is compared to currently used, widely used algorithms in the industry. This technique aims to enhance the encryption procedure and complicate the cryptanalysis procedure. The proposed system provided a better result in accuracy, efficiency, and encryption when compared with existing methods like CNN, C-DSS. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
