AB  - Continuous growth and implementation of the popular Internet of Things (loT) in smart home systems devices have innovated and automated its usage, significantly integrating it. The development of the internet has produced both pros and cons. Indeed, this has led to security challenges that need solutions. Here, the author considers how IoT devices, digital certificates,API keys, and authorization technologies can safeguard smart home network technologies' authentication and user access processes. The proposed study relies on evidence-based techniques that involve data collection, pre-processing, feature extraction, model development, and evaluation of performance outputs to address research problems such as class imbalances and feature extraction. This study contributes to the security trend in smart home technologies by analyzing the appropriate use of digital certificates, API keys, and access controls. The delivery of smart home technologies, security enhancements, and trust in those systems will become possible. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
