AB  - This study aims to track the difficulties faced by senior citizens in today's world and to make a platform titled 'Helping Senior Citizens' for Senior Citizens in several ways. 'Helping Senior Citizens' website would be a one-step solution to many things like companies posting job vacancies for the elderly or specially-abled people and a portal to apply for the same, recreational activities, easy food ordering, and deliveries. This would act as a catalyst in enhancing their quality of life and help them to do what they want to. Also, it would act as a stress buster platform for the users due to the people, they would be able to connect to through this website. Specially- abled people are the most ignored and less privileged. But special attention would be given to their employment opportunities so that the users could feel no less than any normal person out there. This paper articulates the making of this one-stop solution website 'Helping Senior Citizen' using MVC architecture framework and technologies like EJS, MongoDB, Express.js, HTML, and CSS and implementing middlewares for authorization and authentication. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
