AD  - Ltd., Beijing, China
AB  - With the advent of the era of big data, the railway industry urgently needs to adopt efficient and safe distributed storage solutions. However, traditional distributed storage systems are insufficient in terms of data security and compliance. To this end, this article proposes a distributed storage plan based on the national commercial password algorithm (national secret algorithm), based on the Hadoop distributed storage system, and conducts national secret technology transformation. First of all, the SM4 countries secretly plus algorithm, and optimized the flow -type decryption operation during the read and write process, realized the parallel decryption of the data block, greatly improving the transmission efficiency of large files. Secondly, transform the KeyProvider API interface, integrate the national secret key management system, so that it supports the national secret algorithm and implement the key management of the key. In addition, the core functions such as KERBEROS security identity certification and role -based authorization are implemented. This scheme ensures that data can be stored efficiently and safely through the addition of unreasonable storage through the algorithm, which significantly improves the security of data storage, meets the requirements of the national confidentiality degradation, and provides a safe, controllable, high -efficiency and compliance solution for big data storage in the railway industry. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
