AB  - The proceedings contain 96 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Security and Cryptography. The topics include: HydroLab: A Versatile Hydroelectric Power Lab for Security Research and Education; LAMA: Leakage Abuse Attacks Against Microsoft Always Encrypted; Attribute Threat Analysis and Risk Assessment for ABAC and TBAC Systems; fuzzy Vault Security Enhancement Avoid Statistical Biases; Higher Order Leakage Assessment and Neural Network-based Attack on CRYSTALS-Kyber; chiku: Efficient Probabilistic Polynomial Approximations Library; k-Resilient Public Key Authenticated Encryption with Keyword Search; an Extended Method for Transmitting Secret Messages in Textual Documents Based on Paragraph Resizing; High-Speed Pipelined FPGA Implementation of a Robust Steganographic Scheme for Secure Data Communication Systems; Security Analysis for BB84 Key Distillation; On the Implementation of a Lattice-Based DAA for Vanet System; UPCARE: User Privacy-Preserving Cancer Research Platform; MultiVD: A Transformer-based Multitask Approach for Software Vulnerability Detection; Towards Privacy-Preserving Multi-Cloud Identity Management Using SOLID; SCWAD: Automated Pentesting of Web Applications; Linkage Between CVE and ATT&CK with Public Information; dvorak: A Browser Credential Dumping Malware; verifying Artifact Authenticity with Unclonable Optical Tags; a Framework for Federated Analysis of Health Data Using Multiparty Homomorphic Encryption; The Use of the DWARF Debugging Format for the Identification of Potentially Unwanted Applications (PUAs) in WebAssembly Binaries; A Performant Quantum-Resistant KEM for Constrained Hardware: Optimized HQC; OIPM: Access Control Method to Prevent ID/Session Token Abuse on OpenID Connect; a Composition Algebra for Decentralized Enforcement of Access Control Policies with an Application to Vehicular Networks; DYNAMO: Towards Network Attack Campaign Attribution via Density-Aware Active Learning. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights