AD  - Kalasalingam Academy of Research and Education, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Krishnankoil, India
AB  - In the domain of healthcare, ensuring the integrity and confidentiality of medical data is very important. This study proposes an innovative solution that utilizes blockchain technology within a cloud-based framework to address these critical issues. By dispersing and encrypting medical records, the proposed methodology enhances network security, fortifies data privacy, and Enhances confidentiality among healthcare stakeholders. The integration of blockchain not only mitigates network latency but also implements lightweight access controls, fostering the security infrastructure. Empirical findings highlight the efficacy of securely transmitting data through portable devices while upholding the sanctity of personal medical information. This approach holds the potential for advancing data security and privacy in healthcare environment, enabling trust and reliability between patients and providers. Incorporating blockchain technology paves way toward a more resilient and secure healthcare data ecosystem, ensuring the protection and confidentiality of sensitive medical information. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
