AB  - The surge of Internet of Things (IoT) gadgets and cloud-based applications has been increasing the pressure to manage data reliability and security in digital space. This abstract presents examining new techniques for the detection of security among cloud web applications with the capabilities of IoT. Through the equipment of IoT devices, there will be the enhancement of real-time monitoring and detection of safety threats in cloud-based applications that are Internet-based. This synergy enables banks to have access to a variety of data sources, that is, both internal and external data. It makes the collection of large volumes of data possible, and so the banks have a good picture of the environment in which the application runs. With the use of machine learning and AI algorithms in the background, the existing anomalies and known potential vulnerabilities can be found fast, hence paving the way for proactive remediation of the present and future threats. Besides, the sensor through IoT can be utilised to measure physical security areas, which include environmental conditions and access control device integrity, and they make sure provision of security to cloud web applications. A single security architecture that utilises IoT and cloud technologies will allow the organisations to have robust defences, enhanced data protection, and a diminishing risk level, thus keeping the digital services in a trusted and dependable state in an always advanced threat environment. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
