AB  - CloudCraft represents a novel approach to web-based resume management systems, leveraging the power of cloud computing for dynamic deployment and customizable user experiences. Earlier the Resume Builder websites were not capable of providing drag and drop features of customizing the content like User Bio, Education Details, Work Experience etc. This is where our CloudCraft Solution come into picture where we overcome this problem by providing drag and drop features using JavaScript's Functions and Event Listeners. This paper also explores the integration of CloudCraft with AWS, providing users with a seamless and flexible platform to create, customize, and personalize resumes. The research delves into the architecture of the CloudCraft project, emphasizing its innovative use of Docker for containerization and AWS for scalable deployment. The user-centric design allows individuals to tailor their resumes effortlessly, enhancing their job application process. Security measures, including password encryption and JSON Web Tokens (JWT), ensure a secure client-server communication. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
