AB  - This paper presents a dynamic control strategy for high concurrency access with priority in electricity market businesses. The strategy integrates advanced information technology methods with a deep understanding of electricity market business characteristics to ensure the system can rapidly respond and accurately process various businesses, especially those with higher priority in electricity market transactions, in a high concurrency environment. The proposed strategy includes a business priority recognition and mapping mechanism, a priority-based dynamic scheduling algorithm, and a multi-level concurrency control strategy. The implementation of the strategy utilizes a microservices architecture, with services independently deployed, scaled, and maintained. The strategy was deployed and tested in a simulation test environment, with the results demonstrating its effectiveness in handling high concurrency access and improving system throughput, response time, and resource utilization. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
