AB  - This paper explores the design and development of an application to address the challenges bloggers face in managing their online presence across multiple blogging platforms. The proposed application offers a centralized and user-friendly interface to streamline the process of managing online presence. It employs OAuth 2.0 authentication for secure login and utilizes APIs provided by various blogging platforms to enable functionalities such as posting content and retrieving comments. It incorporates sentiment analysis to categorize comments and provides a comprehensive comment management system for bloggers to gain insights into audience reception. This paper also discusses the architecture, methodology, results, merits, and demerits. Their findings contribute to online presence management, providing practical solutions for bloggers to save time, increase productivity, and enhance audience engagement. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
