AB  - In recent years, the use of cloud computing has grown in popularity, as organizations look to take advantage of the scalability, flexibility, and cost-effectiveness of this technology. This chapter aims to explore the issue of data privacy in cloud integration, including the various security measures that can be used to safeguard cloud-stored data, as well as the legal and regulatory problems regarding data privacy. In addition, the role of third-party corporations and organizations in preserving data stored in the cloud will be examined, as will the ethical and moral implications of data privacy in cloud integration. Data privacy in cloud integration necessitates the adoption of strong security measures to prevent unauthorized access to sensitive data and ensure compliance with data protection laws. Organizations must carefully assess cloud service providers’ security features and ensure that adequate security steps are in place to safeguard their data. Furthermore, to reduce the risk of data breaches and guarantee data protection in cloud integration, organizations must implement best practises such as data encryption, access controls, and frequent security assessments. Effective communication and cooperation between cloud service providers and their customers is also required to handle any security concerns and ensure confidential data is protected. Furthermore, the talk will discuss the present state of the art and best practises in data science, privacy in cloud incorporation, providing insights and recommendations to businesses contemplating cloud computing. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
