AD  - National Institute of Technology Raipur, Department of Information Technology, Raipur, India
AD  - Manipal University Jaipur, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Jaipur, India
AB  - The Internet of Things (IoT) gives the ability to people and machines to interact and learn from billions of items, including sensors, actuators, services, and other things that are connected to the Internet. The services provided by IoT are becoming an indispensable part of human life, further, the growth in the number of IoT devices is predicted to increase exponentially in the next few years. However, the IoT network consists of a variety of different types of devices being placed in heterogeneous environments. The data these devices generate contains noise in significant proportion. Also, these devices are vulnerable to various different kinds of attacks, identification of which is a challenging task in itself as they are in large numbers. The detection of faults is necessary for the early stages. Generic methods of authentication and authorization are not sufficient for these devices. Further, we need methods that can detect the attack at an early stage based on previous patterns and alert the system at the right time. In recent years machine learning and deep learning (ML/DL) algorithms have advanced considerably from being an experimental project in the research community to being applied in industry-standard applications. These algorithms have the potential to be better than simple security methods in providing intelligence to the system. In this article, we have reviewed various ML/DL algorithms with their advantages, and disadvantages, and how they can be applied in securing IoTs. Initially, a detailed overview of IoT, components, and applications are presented. After that, we present an overview of various threats, and attack methods are discussed with the probable ML/DL solutions. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
