AB  - The way we interact with the world around us has been totally revolutionized by the Internet of Things (IoT) by allowing for greater automation and connectivity. However, the continuously increased number of IoT devices increases the potential for security vulnerability. With the use of cloud technology, IoT offers a number of benefits including scalability, flexibility, and cost-effectiveness but it also presents unique security challenges. This chapter explores the current state of cloud security in IoT including common threats and attack vectors, and examines the various security measures that can be implemented to mitigate these risks. Key topics discussed include encryption, access control, authentication, and secure communication protocol. Additionally, the chapter highlights the importance of continuous monitoring and threat detection in maintaining the security of cloud-based IoT systems. By understanding the security risks and implementing appropriate safeguards, organizations can maximize the benefits of cloud technology in IoT while minimizing the potential for security breaches. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
