AB  - A cloud-based system called Health Information Exchange (HIE) is. Hosted on Amazon Web Services (AWS). This system provides logins, for doctors, administrators and patients. The primary objective of this work is to revolutionize healthcare data sharing by providing a convenient platform. Patients are empowered to manage their health by selecting their symptoms and receiving disease predictions. AWS is utilized to orchestrate the cloud-based infrastructure, which includes SageMaker for constructing machine learning models RDS for a PostgreSQL database, EC2 for hosting the Django server, Lambda for deploying machine learning model APIs CloudWatch for resource monitoring and IAM, for access control. The core element of this system is the implementation of a classification framework that optimizes the organization and retrieval of data. This innovative approach enhances data accessibility while streamlining healthcare processes to facilitate decision making and patient care. By integrating AWS services, it also creates a scalable foundation that supports the growth of a dynamic retail environment. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
