AB  - The proceedings contain 93 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Research in Computer Security. The topics include: Curveball+: Exploring Curveball-Like Vulnerabilities of Implicit Certificate Validation; Malware Classification Using Open Set Recognition and HTTP Protocol Requests; static Semantics Reconstruction for Enhancing JavaScript-WebAssembly Multilingual Malware Detection; A New Model for Testing IPv6 Fragment Handling; trajectory Hiding and Sharing for Supply Chains with Differential Privacy; A User-Centric Approach to API Delegations: Enforcing Privacy Policies on OAuth Delegations; traffic Analysis by Adversaries with Partial Visibility; learning Markov Chain Models from Sequential Data Under Local Differential Privacy; achilles’ Heels: Vulnerable Record Identification in Synthetic Data Publishing; Peering into the Darkness: The Use of UTRS in Combating DDoS Attacks; Enforcing the GDPR; identity-Based Matchmaking Encryption with Enhanced Privacy – A Generic Construction with Practical Instantiations; Item-Oriented Personalized LDP for Discrete Distribution Estimation; intelligent Zigbee Protocol Fuzzing via Constraint-Field Dependency Inference; FSmell: Recognizing Inline Function in Binary Code; LFuzz: Exploiting Locality-Enabled Techniques for File-System Fuzzing; protocol Dialects as Formal Patterns; ResolFuzz: Differential Fuzzing of DNS Resolvers; fingerprinting of Cellular Infrastructure Based on Broadcast Information; One IDS Is Not Enough! Exploring Ensemble Learning for Industrial Intrusion Detection; evaluating the Security Posture of 5G Networks by Combining State Auditing and Event Monitoring; privMail: A Privacy-Preserving Framework for Secure Emails; towards Efficient Privacy-Preserving Deep Packet Inspection. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
