AB  - The union of cloud computing and cyber security has become progressively important as organizations rely on cloud- based services for their daily functionalities. Explores the practical applications of this amalgamation, specifically in terms of the pros and cons of incorporating cyber security measures in cloud computing environments. Security of cloud computing and the potential benefits of facilitating cyber security measures. These beneficiaries include refined data protection, increase in transparency and control over network activity, and reduced risk of data breaches. Explores different security models and technologies used in cloud computing environments which includes access control, encryption techniques, and surveillance. Cyber security practices and strategies by cloud computing, including the shift towards risk management and the need for collaboration between cloud providers and customers. Cyber security in cloud computing and provides better insights into best practices for ensuring secure cloud environment. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
