AB  - As cloud computing becomes increasingly integrated into modern IT infrastructure, cloud-based data processing and storage security are pressing concerns. This paper delves into the complex issues surrounding cloud data security, identifying and analyzing potential solutions. It thoroughly examines the challenges inherent in cloud environments, including insider threats, data breaches, and infrastructure-sharing vulnerabilities. The paper evaluates various encryption methods used to safeguard data, assessing their efficiency and performance impact. Furthermore, it explores key management strategies, access control mechanisms, and regulatory compliance. This paper concludes by exploring cutting-edge developments in cloud data security, including the impact of quantum computing on cryptographic algorithms, the emergence of postquantum cryptography, and the application of A I and machine learning to enhance cloud security measures. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
