AD  - Siddharth Institute of Engineering & Technology, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Puttur, India
AB  - Elastic, on-demand, and completely managed computer system resources and services are some of the highly alluring aspects of cloud computing. Several challenges include not being able to access data entering or leaving cloud services, data theft and misuse, lack of control over access to sensitive data, and advanced threats including distributed denial of service attacks (DDoS) and virtual machine escape. DDoS assaults are among of the most popular. This title demonstrates an innovative architecture that combines the strengths of neural networks and fuzzy neural networks with a well-posed stacking sparse AutoEncoder (AE) for feature learning. The result is an incredibly powerful hybrid that can distinguish between DDoS attack and regular network traffic. This AEF proposal's enhancements result in a smaller network that prevents overfitting by employing a fuzzy expert approach, reduced reconstruction error, and prevented exploding and vanishing gradients. Using performance criteria like detection precision, accuracy, recall, and F1-Score, a comparison between the suggested method and ten cutting-edge techniques will be carried out. To validate the results, experiments will be run on regular NSL-KDD datasets. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
