AD  - Kalinga Institute of Industrial Technology, Bhubaneswar, School of Computer Engineering, Bhubaneswar, India
AD  - Aryan Institute of Engineering and Technology, Department of CSE, Bhubaneswar, India
AB  - Encryption and decryption are essential in cloud-based systems, and it's vital to ensure they run efficiently. This paper introduces a new method called CloudSecurePath (cSp) to optimize the execution paths of these tasks using Ant Colony Optimization (ACO) and Key-Policy Attribute-Based Encryption (KP-ABE). The ACO algorithm identifies the most efficient resource sequences (such as virtual machines, containers, serverless functions) for encryption and decryption. In the ACO algorithm, ants represent different resource paths, evaluating each path based on execution time and resource use. Pheromone trails are updated to guide future ants to the best paths, and the algorithm runs continuously to adapt to changes in the cloud environment. To further improve security, the approach integrates KP-ABE, which provides fine-grained access control, ensuring only authorized entities can access encrypted data. Combining ACO-based path optimization with KP-ABE results in a robust, adaptive solution for secure and efficient encryption/decryption in cloud systems. The paper details the ACO-based path optimization algorithm, covering its initialization, ant exploration, pheromone updating, and convergence checking. It also discusses about implementing the optimal path and the continuous optimization process. This approach is designed to be scalable and adaptable, making it suitable for various cloud applications needing secure and efficient encryption and decryption. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
