AB  - Cloud computing is changing the IT infrastructure by providing easy-to-use and accessible data over the internet. Although cloud technology is widely used in many different areas, ensuring the security of the cloud is still very difficult. This content explores the complexities of cloud computing security, including technological advances, challenges, and opportunities. Data breaches, insider threats, and compliance challenges are challenging for effective protections such as authentication, authorization, and encryption to help maintain data integrity and security. Blockchain and zero trust architecture are essential to increase security by redefining trust models and access restrictions in the cloud. Regulatory compliance such as GDPR, HIPAA, and ISO/IEC 27001 underscore the importance of tying security measures to legal obligations and providing stringent requirements for service providers' cloud and customer. Service Level Agreements (SLAs) help define and explain the security of service providers and customers. They suggest methods for problem solving and service delivery. This brief concludes by highlighting the ever-changing nature of climate security challenges and the urgent need for adaptive security solutions to regularly mitigate these risks. It provides the truly holistic view needed to understand and manage the complexity of cloud security systems. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
