AB  - This research investigates the creation of a hotel booking application using the MERN (MongoDB, Express.js, React.js, Node.js) stack and Context API. The focus is on leveraging advanced technologies to enhance user experience and booking efficiency. Key factors analyzed include system quality, service quality, customer loyalty, and the role of virtual reality in online bookings (Nair, 2022; Zhang & Wang, 2021). The backend employs Node.js and Express.js for secure, efficient API management, while MongoDB stores user data, hotel details, and reservations flexibly (Jayawardena et al., 2022). Essential features include secure user authentication, role-based access control, comprehensive hotel and room management, conflict-free booking, user dashboards, and administrative controls (Taylor & Evans, 2021). The study also explores the integration of blockchain technology, machine learning, and electronic word-of-mouth in the hotel sector (Smith & Brown, 2021; Davis & Garcia, 2020). This paper aims to provide insights into improving booking processes, reducing cancellations, and increasing hotel revenues (Wilson & Martin, 2021). © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
