AD  - Galgotias University, Greater Noida, India
AB  - Due to the integration of cloud computing with ad hoc networks and the growing use of wireless networks, ad hoc security in cloud computing has emerged as a critical issue. Specially appointed networks are remote organizations made on the fly with next to no decent framework, and they are powerless against different security assaults. Authentication and access control, encryption and confidentiality, intrusion detection, scalability, privacy, and energy efficiency are just a few of the robust security measures that must be put into place when ad hoc networks and cloud computing are combined. Access control policies control who can access network resources, while authentication and access control ensure that only authorized users can do so. Data transmitted over a network can be kept confidential using encryption algorithms like AES, RSA, and ECC. In the event of a security breach, intrusion detection systems (IDS) can be used to monitor the network for suspicious activity and notify the network administrator. The network's scalability, privacy, and energy efficiency can all be ensured by employing lightweight encryption algorithms, privacy-preserving mechanisms, and energy-efficient security mechanisms. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
