AB  - This academic investigation offers a thorough exploration of API security challenges in the Healthcare sector. Through a meticulous review of existing literature, it identifies vulnerabilities and threats, including complex authentication issues, data leakage risks, injection attacks, and weaknesses in access control. The study also points out deficiencies in current security practices, such as improper documentation and tracking protocols. This research provides critical observation for improving healthcare API security and protecting patient data. By lobbying for reliable security practices, Key Players can successfully address these risks. Finally, this paper sheds light on the API security concerns in healthcare, allowing organizations to strengthen healthcare APIs and preserve sensitive patient information, with success validated by quantitative findings. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
