AB  - In order to realize the network security of open platform SaaS applications, avoid user data leakage and data tampering, and improve the security protection ability of application services, this research uses the application gateway based on Spring Gateway and Spring Security to build a user rights model by using RBAC principle, and realizes the technology-controllable link encryption and digital signature scheme by SM2, SM3 and SM4 national secret algorithms. The application gateway records access logs uniformly, and forms an application gateway with certain security protection ability, which has user authentication, controllable access rights, data transmission encryption and traceability after access. By introducing this application gateway, the network security capability of the open platform can be enhanced, and at the same time, the development intrusion of platform services can be avoided. It is compatible with business micro-services with different architectures and different development languages, which is conducive to the formation of unified service security protection. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
