AD  - Alagappa University, Department of Computational Logistics, Karaikudi, India
AB  - In this generation, cloud computing is widely supported for all new technologies in the form of the largest virtual storage device. If the system contains a large amount of data, it is not possible to store or share the local files on the system, so then, using the cloud. Because the cloud is the biggest virtual storage device, you use someone else's cloud server to host, process, or store the data. If you want to store and access any information connected to the cloud and retrieve the data from wherever you store it, previously everything was on our local system, but now, drastically increasing the concept of information in cloud computing, So it will be aware of everyone, flexible to use, and available for everyone to access whenever or wherever. The processing of data on the cloud has several issues, particularly those related to security and privacy since it is a new technology. Data loss software, secured file systems, and security apps may all help to lessen the problems associated with cloud computing. The data control procedures in the cloud server paradigm are provided via attribute-based cryptography. Depending on the rules governing access control, ABE encrypts data at the granular level. To authenticate an external user, the Privacy Preserving Access Control Policy (PPAC) is employed. Data is converted to cipher text and stored on the cloud server. Access control policy generates the keys to prevent unauthorized users. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
