UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85185379539&doi=10.1109%2FICTACS59847.2023.10390302&partnerID=40&md5=8e6fb4616c82ae93356a6cf539b9a149
AD  - Chandigarh University, Department of CSE, Mohali, India
AB  - Critical data and systems are now more frequently kept and analyzed in the cloud as a result of the cloud computing industry's quick development. As enterprises trust valuable information to third-party service providers, this presents significant security risks. This article's goal is to outline the security issues that cloud computing raises and suggest solutions that safeguard private information and systems in cloud-based environments for businesses. The article will give a brief overview of cloud computing along with its numerous security issues, such as insider threats, data privacy, and data breaches. The study will next look at several measures, such as the use of encryption, control over access, and audits, to safeguard sensitive data and infrastructure in the cloud. The paper will also discuss how cloud service providers can help secure the cloud environment and what certifications and compliance rules businesses must follow while using the cloud. The final section of the study will cover cloud security's prospects and potential developments in the years to come. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
