AD  - University of Technology Bahrain, College of Computer Studies, Salmabad, Bahrain
AB  - The use of Internet and cloud storage is increasing daily and hence issues related to cloud security are also increasing day-by-day. In this research, we are trying to find a solution that will protect the data integrity and security of cloud data transfers and storage. Here we analyze the Key Policy-Attribute Based Encryption (KP-ABE) and Hierarchical Set Based Attribute based Encryption (HASBE) to find the speed of Execution Time, Data Security Rate, Data Integrity Rate and Space complexity. From the study we concluded that HASBE has a more powerful algorithm with less execution time, more secure and more integrated with less space complexity. HASBE has an ordered hierarchical structure of aligning cloud data. Both KP-ABE and HASBE are based on Attribute encryption where unique attributes like telephone number, email-id, personal id number which can identify a person uniquely will be used. Among the two algorithms it is found that HASBE is more efficient. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
