AD  - Galgo3as University, Greater Noida, India
AB  - Cloud computing has evolved as an effective model for delivering computing resources and services over the Internet. While it has many advantages, such as scalability and cost-effectiveness, the security of data stored and processed in the cloud is still a key worry. This article provides an in-depth examination of data security in cloud computing, emphasising the different difficulties, solutions, and emerging trends in this subject. We investigate the most serious threats to data security, such as unauthorised access, data breaches, and insider attacks, as well as the tactics and mechanisms used to minimise these risks. Furthermore, we cover developments in encryption, access control, authentication, and other security methods that improve the security of sensitive data in the cloud. This review's goal is to evaluate and summarise available studies. © 2023 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
