AD  - Lovely Professional University, Phagwara, India
AB  - The Internet has become such an important part of people's lives that they can't live without it. It helps people with business, education, and entertainment, among other things, on individual machines or over the network in the cloud environment. Internet applications are used by both organizations and clients for business tasks using cloud computing. But as the Internet becomes more popular, there is a chance of attacks on an individual system or an organization's service unavailability in the cloud computing environment. The organization must be protected from such known or unknown attacks. Intrusion is an attempt to attack on classification, accessibility, and trustworthiness. It is a set of practices that try to breach into the security of an organization's resources in different ways, such as outside attacks, inside attacks, network-based attacks, data collection, information collection, denial of service, etc. Due to cost and complexity, no system can be fully protected, so programmers will eventually figure out how to break into our systemand look at network information to find potential attackers. Conventional means for preventing intrusions, such as access control list, firewalls, and encryption improvements, have not been able to protect organizations and systems from increasingly complex attacks and harmful software. A key part of any security system helps find threats before they do real damage. Intrusion Detection System (IDS) is a mix of hardware, software, methods, or both, and its job is to find expected changes in network information. In the cloud environment the API logs and authentication are monitored apart from implementing IDS for network layer and host-based security. © 2023 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
