AD  - China Electronic Product Reliability and Environmental Testing Research Institute, Guangzhou, China
AB  - With the continuous development of software engineering, a large number of functions that used to be completed by hardware are now controlled and completed by software. Iot cloud platforms are also increasingly dependent on software. Once the software fails or runs abnormally, the system failure caused by it may directly lead to the hardware failure, resulting in serious security problems. Under the premise of ensuring functional safety, the software of the Iot cloud platform should meet the reusability of the code and meet the needs of the rapid development of the Iot cloud platform through modularization and componentization. This paper designs a security component sharing strategy for the Iot cloud platform, which avoids some common problems caused by traditional access control strategies while realizing dynamic and flexible identity management, and reduces certain economic and social costs. © 2023 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
