AB  - Internet of Things (IoT) and its security has gained the attention of various researchers in recent times The present government, public or organizations depend upon the technology while comparing to 19th century. So per better quality and development of technology we need public needs and requirements. To find that requirement we need some IOT tools The Internet of Things (IoT) refers to a group of tangible items, such as structures, machines, and automobiles, that have been outfitted with electronic components, software programs, and sensing apparatuses. These entities are capable of gathering and sharing data as they are linked to the internet. IoT is transforming the way companies do business by connecting people, processes, data, and things to create a more intelligent and efficient environment. IoT is used in many applications, such as smart homes, connected cars, and smart cities. IoT security is a key concern for businesses, as connected devices are vulnerable to malicious attacks. Security measures must be taken to protect the data and prevent unauthorized access. These measures include encryption, authentication, and access control. Companies should also use measures such as vulnerability scans and patch management to ensure that all devices are secure. Additionally, businesses should be aware of any potential security risks associated with new technologies. By taking the necessary steps to secure IoT devices, businesses can ensure that they are protected from malicious attacks. © 2023 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
