TI  - A Fine-Grained Data Encryption Scheme Based on Shortest Vector Problem in the Cloud Computing Environment
PY  - 2023
SP  - 809
EP  - 814
DO  - 10.1109/ICSIP57908.2023.10270961
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/inward/record.uri?eid=2-s2.0-85174694485&doi=10.1109%2FICSIP57908.2023.10270961&partnerID=40&md5=75c77abcd9814363b44a38ad2540aede
AD  - Southeast University, School of Cyber Science and Engineering, Nanjing, China
AB  - Lattice-based encryption is a promising public key cryptography to resist quantum computing attacks. Simultaneously, due to the need for fine-grained access control in cloud environments, it is crucial to do the research on attribute-based encryption (ABE). However, researches on ABE algorithm have some problems such as not having mechanisms secure enough to defend against quantum computing attacks with high decryption accuracy, having vulnerabilities to collusion attacks and lacking of attribute revocation mechanism. In order to solve the above problems, we propose a new data encryption scheme with fine-grained access control based on the shortest vector problem in the cloud computing environment (DES-SVP). We formally prove that our DES-SVP scheme can resist quantum computing attacks and can resist collusion attacks between users. We reduce our DES-SVP scheme to the problem of finding a short vector in a lattice so that our scheme can withstand quantum computing attacks. Finally, the performance analysis shows that our DES-SVP scheme can achieve efficient results comparing with other related works. © 2023 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
