AB  - The proceedings contain 64 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Expert Clouds and Applications. The topics include: A Detailed Survey on Network Intrusion Detection in Cloud Using Different Techniques; evaluation of Security of Cloud Deployment Models in Electronic Health Records; leasing in IaaS Cloud Using Queuing Model; Resource Allocation Using MISO-NOMA Scheme with Clustering Technique; Resource Request Handling Mechanisms for Effective VM Placements in Cloud Environment; self-adaptive Hadoop Cluster for Data Analysis Applications; sustainable Cloud Computing in the Supply Chains; task Scheduling in Fog Assisted Cloud Environment Using Hybrid Metaheuristic Algorithm; Trust Model for Cloud Using Weighted KNN Classification for Better User Access Control; a Case Study of IoT-Based Biometric Cyber Security Systems Focused on the Banking Sector; Blockchain Security Through SHA-512 Algorithm Implementation Using Python with NB-IoT Deployment in Food Supply Chain; adoption of Network Function Virtualization Technology in Education; IOT-Based Whip-Smart Trash Bin Using LoRa WAN; monitoring of Wireless Network System-Based Autonomous Farming Using IoT Protocols; a Brief Survey on Enhanced Quality of Service Mechanisms in Wireless Sensor Network for Secure Data Transmission; A Mobile Application Model for Differently Abled Using CNN, RNN and NLP; a Survey Paper: On Path Planning Strategies Based on Classical and Heuristic Methods; Actual Problems and Analysis of Anti-avoidance Tax Measures in the EAEU and EU Countries in the Context of Digitalization of the Economy; an Alternative Approach to Smart Air Conditioner with Multiple Power Sources; Appointment Scheduler for VIP Using Python and Twilio; deep Learning-Based Facial Emotion Analysis. © 2023 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
