AB  - The objective of this chapter is to provide a concise overview of KIS.API, which can be used for effective communication with external applications. In particular, the chapter starts with a general overview of KIS.API along with preliminary steps pertaining to KIS.API user registration and authorization in KIS.MANAGER. Subsequently, it is shown how to access essential functionalities explained in the preceding chapters through the KIS.API framework. Thus, the reader will be able to access the asset and user groups as well as the assets themselves. Another crucial point of this chapter is concerned with accessing data through Datapoints as well as calculated Datapoints and KPIs. Subsequently, the mechanism of Rule engine is confronted with KIS.API. In particular, it is show how to access information about the rules designed in KIS.MANGER as well as how to trigger the rules from external applications. With all the above-listed components, the concept of websockets is introduced along with sample applications concerning two-way communication with KIS.ME. Finally, the chapter is summarized with a set of training exercises concerning KIS.API-oriented skills. © 2023 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
