AD  - SRM Institute of Science and Technology, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Kattankulathur, India
AB  - As technology advances, the number of devices that connect to the internet has expanded significantly, necessitating efficient and swift data transfer. In the past years, cloud computing has shown to be a dependable and economical method of interconnecting devices to the Internet. With the growth of real time applications in wireless devices the cloud servers are unable to respond quickly enough. Some applications that require lowlatency, effective methods, require more mobility, precision, elasticity, energy efficiency, and dependability are not so much supported by cloud computing. Edge computing provides cloud computing services which make the devices closer to the end users for reliable applications. Surveillance, virtual reality, and real-time traffic monitoring are just a few examples of internet-enabled applications that necessitate fast processing and response times. Edge computing meets the above-mentioned application needs by bringing computation to the network's edge. Cloudlets, fog computing, and mobile edge computing are three edge computing technologies that can be used to solve cloud computing difficulties. Edge computing is a cloud extension that provides substantial processing and storage capabilities to the network's edge, forming an edge layer close to the internet of things end devices. As a result, many computation-intensive and resource-intensive tasks can be offloaded from resource-constrained end devices to the resource-rich edge layer. This new computing paradigm improves system performance while decreasing resource limitations at IoT endpoints at the same time. A new platform for developing and delivering IoT security solutions is also included. Novel edge-based IoT security solutions have been investigated. These approaches include edge-based security architecture designs, firewalls, intrusion detection systems, authentication and authorization procedures, and privacypreserving tactics, to name a few. © 2023 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
