AD  - Shipbome Equipment Research and Test Center, Kunming, China
AB  - Permission management is an important part of software system, which is very important to ensure the security of application system resources and information. Based on the latest vuetify3.0 framework, this paper has designed and implemented a lightweight permission management software applied to the workshop information system, which can realize the functions of role permission allocation, query and modification. The software uses modular thinking to separately design the allocation, query and modification functions of role permissions. The front-end uses simple web page design so that the system administrator can quickly and repeatedly switch between the permission allocation, query and modification interfaces. The system administrator's modification information of permissions will be uploaded in real time and saved to the background server, so that the permission management function can take effect in real time. Through a large number of experiments, this paper shows that the software has well realized the permission management function in the workshop information system, and has the advantages of simple operation, high execution efficiency, strong stability and good scalability. © 2023 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
