AD  - China Southern Power Grid, Guangzhou, China
AB  - Aiming at the problem that the current power monitoring system front-end computer has poor access control capability, which leads to the long time-consuming of data sending and receiving, a front-end computer configuration method for power monitoring system based on cloud computing access control is designed. The BQ4011YMA-100 chip is selected as the core chip of the front-end computer, and the peripheral circuit and network interface of the chip are set. Build a cloud computing access control model, analyze the reliability of data receiving nodes according to the AHP, and control access security. Set the front-end data transceiver program to realize the front-end configuration data transceiver function of the power monitoring system. So far, the design of the front-end computer configuration method of the power monitoring system based on cloud computing access control is completed. Build a test link to analyze the front-end function after this configuration method is used. The test results show that this configuration method can shorten the data sending and receiving time to a certain extent and improve the performance of the system. © 2023 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
