AB  - In the growth trend of mobile Internet, with the continuous innovation of technology, more and more people begin to use mobile phones and other devices to live. At the same time, people's demand for information resources is increasing. In the traditional sense, web refers to the large amount of content data on the web page. This paper introduces the design and implementation of cross platform mobile Internet Project Based on large data interaction. The system provides real-time, efficient and reliable access control for intelligent terminals. Users can browse web content and other operations through mobile apps. The client can set and deploy on any platform according to its own needs. At the same time, it will automatically generate a page to display in the corresponding interface. After receiving the request, the server will feed back the results to the user. Finally, the performance of the system is tested. The test results show that the cross platform web system based on big data interaction has high compatibility, security and fast running speed, which shows that the performance of the system can meet the needs of users. © 2023 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
