AD  - Ruhr-Universitat Bochum, Chair for Network and Data Security, Bochum, Germany
AB  - Single Sign-On protocols (SSO) are used to grant a web user authenticated access to many web applications after a single manual login. On the client side, SSO protocols like OAuth, OpenID Connect, or SAML rely on standard web browser features. The blueprint for modern SSO protocols is the Kerberos protocol [56] described in chapter 14. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
