AB  - Security attacks are increasingly diverse and complex so ensuring security properties has become an important criterion in evaluating the quality of software systems. Besides, attribute-based access control (ABAC) is widely applied to ensure the security properties of software systems, especially large-scale and complex systems. However, deploying this security policy is always likely to contain potential security flaws that are the causes of the failures to guarantee customer security requirements, especially at the programming stage. In this paper, we introduce an approach to check the compliance of implemented ABAC policy with the Spring Security framework of a web application and its specification automatically. The proposal helps developers in detecting security breach situations that lead to disrupting the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of application systems. © 2022 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
