AB  - The proceedings contain 121 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Wireless Communications, Networking and Applications. The topics include: Cross-Knowledge Graph Entity Alignment via Neural Tensor Network; Unsupervised MRI Images Denoising via Decoupled Expression; The Method for Micro Expression Recognition Based on Improved Light-Weight CNN; a Fully-Nested Encoder-Decoder Framework for Anomaly Detection; development of Deep Learning Algorithms, Frameworks and Hardwares; orchard Energy Management to Improve Fruit Quality Based on the Internet of Things; CTran_DA: Combine CNN with Transformer to Detect Anomalies in Transmission Equipment Images; from Data Literacy to Co-design Environmental Monitoring Innovations and Civic Action; a Novel Home Safety IoT Monitoring Method Based on ZigBee Networking; technological Intervention of Sleep Apnea Based on Semantic Interoperability; Multidimensional Data Analysis Based on LOGIT Model; five Application Modes of Mobile Government; a Storage Scheme for Access Control Record Based on Consortium Blockchain; a Formalization of Topological Spaces in Coq; A Method of UAV Formation Transformation Based on Reinforcement Learning Multi-agent; design and Implementation of Full Adder Circuit Based on Memristor; exploration of Non-legacy Creative Product Development Based on Information Technology; Multivariate Passenger Flow Forecast Based on ACLB Model; an Insight into Load Balancing in Cloud Computing; new Tendencies in Regulating Personal Data. Can We Achieve Balance?; the Ground-State Potential Energy Surface of F-Li<inf>2</inf> Polymer; An Effective GAN-Based Multi-classification Approach for Financial Time Series; certificateless Identity Management and Authentication Scheme Based on Blockchain Technology; from Information Resources Push to Service Aggregation: The Development Trend of Mobile Government Service; preface. © 2022 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
