AB  - Currently, news has revealed powerful attackers who can breach the confidentiality of data by means of secretly obtaining cryptographic keys. The keys are obtained through threats within software cryptography. When the encryption key gets exposed, the lone reasonable act is used for maintaining the confidentiality of data to confine the attacker access to the ciphertext. The Confining attacker's access is accomplished using widening blocks for ciphertext over servers within several administrative domains. Thus, presuming the adversary will not pose danger. However, once encryption of data is done using prevalent designs then the process of encryption key adversary will be compromised with a single server as it will decrypt to perform encryption over the blocks of ciphertext. An adversary perceives the encryption key and will possess it for accessing a huge portion of the ciphertext blocks. The present research paper will review the existing encryption-decryption techniques for achieving Secure, Scalable, and Fine-grained Data Access Control in Cloud Computing. © 2022 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
