AD  - Beijing University of Posts and Telecommunications, Beijing, China
AB  - Because of the ever-increasing need of data sharing among multiple parties, data security in cloud storage becomes a huge challenge. Consider data sharing as a complicated scenario and the time is a key factor in many access control applications, more flexible access control policies are needed. Our work proposes a new method named as TSM, which belongs to time-sensitive multi-authority attribute-based encryption, adding a time-domain attribute to attribute-based encryption. Data owners can pre-set the specific time of each file and upload ciphertext to the cloud storage platform, and data users cannot decrypt the ciphertext until the specific time reaches. Reaching a tradeoff of efficiency and security, TSM is efficient and can update time attributes with low storage cost, which is suitable for data sharing in time-sensitive access control scenarios. This paper finally proves that TSM is secure under q-BDHE. Both theoretical analysis and experimental results show that TSM can indeed enhance data security efficiently with low cost. © 2022 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
