AB  - In the age of IoT, access control of smart objects and services has become more important than ever. However, existing access control mechanisms are not flexible enough to cover the demands in many of the real use cases in IoT scenarios. For instance, visitors of IoT-enabled buildings may need to use the IoT facilities of the room they visit, for a limited period of time. In order to realize such flexibility in access control of IoT, we propose AFWA, an access control framework that seamlessly integrates Web API in access control. By integrating Web API in access control, event information from Calendar API, for example, can be used for judging access permissions of IoT devices. © 2022 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
