AB  - The proceedings contain 15 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Computer Science, Electrical and Electronic Engineering. The topics include: Velocity-Based Control of Piston Trajectory in a Free-Piston Linear Electric Generator by Load Current Modulation; GBI-Based Wireless Home Automation System Using IoT; embedded Machine Learning on a Programmable Neuromorphic Platform; investigation on Two Dimensional Photonic Crystal Based All Optical Logic Gates; miniaturized Multiband Metamaterial Antenna for 5G Applications; model-Based Testing of Access Control Requirement in Multi-tenant Application: An Extensive Life Cycle; survivable Biconnected Topology for Yemen’s Optical Network; a Study on Electric Field Distribution in Polymeric Insulator Using Finite Element Method; Modelling and Simulation of Building-Integrated Photovoltaics (BIPV) Installations in Swinburne University; ant Colony Optimization Algorithms for Routing in Wireless Sensor Networks: A Review; Analyzing the Effects of Corona Ring Material and Dimensions on the Electric Field Distribution of 132 kV Glass Insulator String Using 2-D FEM; Ultra-Compact All-Optical NAND Logic Gates Based on 4 × 4 MMI Coupler Using Silicon Hybrid Plasmonic Waveguides; Microstrip Patch Antenna Arrays Design for 5G Wireless Backhaul Application at 3.5 GHz. © 2022 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
