AD  - ABES Institute of Technology, Department of IT, Ghaziabad, India
AB  - Online healthcare system allows patients to remotely access the required medical history whenever required. Accessing the patient records as well as medical history associated with the diagnosis is beneficial not only for patients but also for healthcare personnel. But this practice may lead to major security and privacy concerns of patient’s private data, e.g., no patient would like to reveal the health-related data which may cause trouble in his/her personal life as well as the professional life. For electronic health record (EHR) adaptation, the major elements are laws and regulations, monetary inducement and hurdles, technology state, and corporation effect. Emerging technologies like blockchain, cloud computing, and IoT have a vital role in healthcare information systems. In this chapter, I have discussed several privacy and security issues and solutions for healthcare informatics. © 2022 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
