AB  - The proceedings contain 90 papers. The special focus in this conference is on ICT for Sustainable Development. The topics include: Family of Friends—A Hostel Utility System; vulnerability Due to Training Order in Split Learning; efficient Attendance Management System Based on Face Recognition; automated Medical Symptoms Summarization and Patient Profiling System; smart Shoe Provides Vision to Visionless Person; Relevance of Disruptive Technologies Led Knowledge Management System and Practices for MSME; empirical Analysis of Static and Dynamic Stopword Generation Approaches; rethinking Access Control Mechanism for Ubiquitous Computing; review of Smart Building Management System; optimal Packet Routing with Multiple Demands and Link Lines; design and Study the Performance of Micro-Strip Patch Antennae for 5G Mobile Communication; mapping and Change Detection of Mangroves Using Remote Sensing and Google Earth Engine: A Case Study; source Code Obfuscation: Novel Technique and Implementation; design and Implementation of Laptop Tracking System Based on Cloud Computing and IoT; Design and Implementation of Women Security System Based on GSM and GPS Technology; a Scalable Framework for High-Performance Computing with Cloud; mango (Mangifera Indica L.) Classification Using Shape, Texture and Convolutional Neural Network Features; modeling Human Tendencies for Password Guessing; leveraging Big Data Analytics for Predictive Policing in India; an Assured Encryption Strategy for Private Data Protection in Hybrid Cloud; reducing Labelled Data Requirement for Pneumonia Segmentation Using Image Augmentations; Sentiment Analysis of COVID-19 Vaccine Rollout in India; feature Extraction for Automatic Grading of Students’ Presentations; monitoring and Assessment of Water Bodies in Madurai Using Geo-Spatial Data; image Captioning Using Ensemble Model. © 2022 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
