AD  - Netaji Subhas University of Technology,East Campus, New Delhi, India
AB  - Access control has become the most necessary requirement to limit unauthorized and privileged access to information systems in cloud computing. Access control models counter the additional security challenges like rules, domain names, job allocation, multi-hosting, and separation of tasks. This paper classifies the conventional and modern access control models which has been utilized to restrain these access flaws by employing a variety of practices and methodologies. It examines the frequent security threats to information confidentiality, integrity, data accessibility, and their approach used for cloud solutions. This paper proposed a priority-based task scheduling access control (PbTAC) model to secure and scheduled access of resources and services rendered to the cloud user. PbTAC model will ensure the job allocation, tasks scheduling, and security of information through its rule policies during transmission between parties. It also helps in reducing system overhead by minimizing the computation and lowering storage cost. © 2025 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
