AB  - IoT constitutes an important area of cyber–physical systems, whose design and programming involve interactions between multiple abstraction layers. This article describes the new AXIOM project IoT node, its hardware architecture, programming environment, and two application scenarios where it may be used. The AXIOM project aims to build a powerful node for the IoT infrastructure. In the context of this project, we have selected two IoT application scenarios: smart video surveillance (SVS) and smart home living (SHL). Those are being used to validate the Xilinx Zynq platforms as a good basis, upon which we can build the services for the IoT. The AXIOM IoT programming environment is based on the task-parallel OmpSs programming model. In the same way, we use OmpSs to leverage the existing accelerated kernels in CUDA and OpenCL, and we are developing the OmpSs@FPGA version. © 2021 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
