AB  - SAAS (Storage as a service) is referred as a significant cloud computing (CC) services that support cloud users (CU) to overcome the bottleneck on constrained assets and extent storage without updating their gadgets. To guarantee the protection privacy of CU, the information is generally outsourced in encrypted format. Nevertheless, encrypted information might produce more storage waste in cloud and complicates the data exchange among authorized users. Even now, some problems exist with encrypted data and deduplication in cloud and storage management. Traditional deduplication methods focus on specific application scenarios, whereas in the cloud, reduplication will be completely controlled by servers or data owners. They might not flexibly fulfill the separate requests obtained from data owners, who rely on sensitivity level of data. In this manuscript, the proposed method flexibly provides the similar time through numerous Cloud service providers [CSPs]. The researchers assesse the execution with security examination, comparison execution. © 2021 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
