AD  - The Open University of Sri Lanka, Department of Electrical & Computer Engineering, Nugegoda, Sri Lanka
AB  - Resource availability and accessibility in fog-to-cloud computing platforms is vital to facilitate delay-critical services. Cloud and fog collaborations for resource sharing can help to meet the service level time-critical requirements by making the available resources accessible. In this paper process management scheme is proposed for secure storage access considering a fog-to-cloud architecture. Failure criteria and service request arrival control are described. The results demonstrate the suitability of the process management scheme to be integrated to the fog-to-cloud architecture. © 2022 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
