AB  - Securing high number of IoT devices and sensors in smart farming ecosystem became a challenge especially when it comes to access control. Traditional approaches for access control mostly rely on a central authority which is a centralised server that is risky as it possesses a single point of failure and could be compromised with malicious attacks. Hence having a centralised model for access control does not seem to be an ideal solution. Meanwhile, blockchain technology, a decentralised Distributed Ledger Technology potentially can be applied to manage the access control. This study aims to propose a secure decentralised access control model using blockchain technology to secure the resources in smart farming ecosystem with a multi-tenant deployment model. © 2021 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
