AB  - The proceedings contain 20 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Quality, Reliability, Security and Robustness in Heterogeneous Networks. The topics include: Towards Secure and Trustworthy Crowdsourcing with Versatile Data Analytics; blockchain for IoT: A Critical Analysis Concerning Performance and Scalability; toward Achieving Unanimity for Implicit Closings in a Trustless System; DBS: Blockchain-Based Privacy-Preserving RBAC in IoT; achieving Fair and Accountable Data Trading Scheme for Educational Multimedia Data Based on Blockchain; a Lightweight Authentication Protocol for 5G Cellular Network Connected Drones; anti-eavesdropping Proportional Fairness Access Control for 5G Networks; preface; FedDICE: A Ransomware Spread Detection in a Distributed Integrated Clinical Environment Using Federated Learning and SDN Based Mitigation; joint Relay Selection and Frequency Allocation for D2D Communications; Chaos and Logistic Map Based Key Generation Technique for AES-Driven IoT Security; A Usability Study of Cryptographic API Design; an S-box Design Using Irreducible Polynomial with Affine Transformation for Lightweight Cipher; The Phantom Gradient Attack: A Study of Replacement Functions for the XOR Function; Topology Validator - Defense Against Topology Poisoning Attack in SDN; towards an Attention-Based Accurate Intrusion Detection Approach; Avoiding VPN Bottlenecks: Exploring Network-Level Client Identity Validation Options; puncturable Search: Enabling Authorized Search in Cross-data Federation. © 2021 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
