AB  - The proceedings contain 31 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Computing and Information Technology. The topics include: Natural Language Processing with “More Than Words – BERT”; automatically Retrieving of Software Specification Requirements Related to Each Actor; reservoir Inflow Time Series Forecasting Using Regression Model with Climate Indices; ADGAS: An Advanced Data Generation for Anomalous Signals; Object Detection with Convolution Neural Networks and Custom-SmallerVGGNet; HFMD Skin Rash Detection Using Convolutional Neural Networks; comparative Study Considering Garbage Classification Using In-Depth Learning Techniques; a Sequenced Edge Grid Image Technique for Sign Language Recognition; a Unified Framework for Saliency Segmentation; intelligent Fruit Recognition System Using Deep Learning; intelligent Interface for Blind Users to Perform Collaborative Activities; Graph NLU Enabled Question Answering System; integrating Graph-Based Document Recommendation in Digital Libraries of Theses Collection; modeling of Aluminum Profile Extrusion Yield: Online Billet Cutting; enhanced Hydrozoan Algorithm with Local Searches for Job-Shop Scheduling Problems; model Predictive Control of a Fed-Batch Enzymatic Hydrolysis Reactor for Processing Lignocellulosic Feedstock; split-Match-Merge Method with Multi-matcher Algorithm to Handle Data Interoperability Problems in Small Farm Management Information System; intelligent Triage Assistant; Development of Physical and Mental Support System Using Communication Robot for Isolated COVID-19 Patients; a Cloud Based Knowledge Sharing System for Traditional Medicines; Design and Development of a Dynamic and Efficient PII Data Loss Prevention System; an Analytical Review of Data Access Control Schemes in Mobile Cloud Computing; Integration of MANET with In-Band SDN Controller; herb Suggestion Model for Treat Disease by Symptoms Using Decision Tree Techniques. © 2021 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
