AB  - Each day the need for cloud computing increases to provide flexible storing and cloud services and according to the users’ wishes. If a certain owner of data wishes to share this data with another user, the security of data will form a complicated problem. In the current research, a secure data sharing and storing system is suggested on the cloud, with offering data secrecy and access control authenticity for data. The suggested model reduces the load on the central management and offers encryption and decryption for the files shared by the users. The suggested system consists of three fundamental entities: cloud service (CS), certificate authority (CA), and users, where CA is the trusted entity to generate keys and distribute them on other entities and to encrypt and decrypt files. © 2021 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
