AB  - The proceedings contain 30 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Security, Privacy, and Anonymity in Computation, Communication, and Storage. The topics include: Improving Deep Neural Network Robustness with Siamese Empowered Adversarial Training; predicting Advanced Persistent Threats for IoT Systems Based on Federated Learning; DFspliter: Data Flow Oriented Program Partitioning Against Data Stitching Attacks; revisiting Attacks and Defenses in Connected and Autonomous Vehicles; an Improved Cryptanalysis Algorithm for Chebyshev Map-Based Discrete Logarithm Problem; reinforcement-Learning Based Network Intrusion Detection with Human Interaction in the Loop; preface; privacy-Preserving and Scalable Data Access Control Based on Self-sovereign Identity Management in Large-Scale Cloud Storage; research on Security of Access Control for Cloud Computing Environment; Research and Development of Privacy Protection of WSN Routing Protocol; apply Quantum Search to the Safety Check for Mono Operational Attribute Based Protection Systems; a Semi-supervised Intrusion Detection Algorithm Based on Auto-encoder; research on Arm TrustZone and Understanding the Security Vulnerability in Its Cache Architecture; scrutinizing Trust and Transparency in Cash on Delivery Systems; expansion Adaptation of Attack-Aware Controller-Link-Switch Cost Minimization Placement in Software-Defined Networking; a Weighted Federated Averaging Framework to Reduce the Negative Influence from the Dishonest Users; i Can Think Like You! Towards Reaction Spoofing Attack on Brainwave-Based Authentication; Cubic Permutation Polynomials-Based Block RLNC Algorithm in Wireless Networks; attention Mechanism Based Adversarial Attack Against Deep Reinforcement Learning; A Lightweight Blockchain-Based Trust Model for Smart Vehicles in VANETs; light Intensity Based IoT Device Positioning for Indoor Monitoring; A Blockchain-Based Reconstruction Framework for UAV Network. © 2021 Elsevier B.V., All right