AB  - Abstract—: Security of modern data architectures implemented in relational DBMS’s is analyzed. The emphasis is placed on inference attacks, which are not prevented by traditional access control methods. Examples of such attacks are given and fundamental approaches to protecting against them are analyzed. The development of special software built and operating on the principles of intellectual data analysis is proposed as a security measure. © 2021 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
