AD  - Lomonosov Moscow State University, Institute of Mechanics, Moscow, Russian Federation
AB  - Information systems providing interactive access for a huge number of users worldwide are exposed to numerous security threats. One of the most significant threats to this sort of systems is the threat of unauthorized access to system resources, leading to the breach of data confidentiality (privacy), data integrity and to the denial of service. The design and implementation of models and algorithms to reduce the risks of realizing such threats and to ensure the prompt response to the incidents is an important problem. In this article we introduce the chain-relational model of access control (ChRelBAC), which was designed and implemented for a large scientometric system. We describe two software tools for supporting the model. Visualization tool presents access control rules in a user-friendly way. Verification tool for the processes of the model integration with the target information system source code identifies the entry points of the system that are not covered by the model. Finally, we discuss the problem of testing the relational model on the real data sets. © 2020 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
