AD  - University of Pembangunan Nasional, Department of Information System, Surabaya, Indonesia
AB  - Wireless network technology provides an opportunity for organizations to provide efficient and integrated information services. Asset Procurement and Management Services Surabaya is one of the organizations tasked with providing asset procurement and management services. The organization has three warehouses located in a city with a considerable distance, and only the central warehouse has an internet network. Implementation of point-to-multipoint network sharing of internet networks from the central warehouse to other warehouses. This study aims to implement a point-to-multipoint based on MikroTik Router to connect internet networks centrally to the three warehouses and manage bandwidth and restrict website access. The point-to-multipoint network is a wireless internet network from one radio access point connected to several radio stations located in several locations that are quite far away, and it is not possible to pass through a network cable. The research method uses the Network Development Life Cycle (NDLC) with analysis, design, simulation, implementation, monitoring, and management. The point-to-multipoint network implementation results provide network access control and bandwidth management for convenience in controlling the network and sharing resources, data, and information. QoS (Quality of Service) testing shows good calculation results of Throughput, Delay, Jitter, and Packet Loss. © 2021 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
