AD  - Rakuten Mobile Inc., India
AB  - This paper gives an overview of the existing problems and requirements for privileged access to network functions in a virtual multi-tenant network. Cloud networks often use already existing solutions, and each solution is individually configured and build for different purposes. This leads to the following problems: First, using a variety of authentication methods leads to an inhomogeneous level of security for the different virtual functions in the network. Second, security policies differ from one solution provider to the other. Third, settings are set on different virtual functions locally and also on different layers of software which makes the authentication methods difficult to maintain. Simultaneously, by exploiting the authentication vulnerabilities, the possibility of attacks may increase. Thus, it is challenging, but crucial providing these network functions with secure access which includes strong authentication and holistic logging, in order to reduce the risk of incidents and detect attacks. © 2021 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
