AB  - Security testing is considered to be a challenging process mainly because from a product context, not all functional testing meant to illustrate consent to its information, safety testing is a type of negative testing that shows that a particular activity isn’t performed in the system. Android's authorization-based security model limits applications to specific properties, but harmful applications can target the system without much difficulty. By analyzing the Android Permission-based Protection Framework and the Android User Permission Framework, a permission model is created to evaluate the application's functional attributes and then provide a test method using the clustering algorithm and network visualization techniques that allow users to choose whether the application that is tested is a potentially dangerous application or not. © 2020 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
