AB  - The proceedings contain 22 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Data and Applications Security and Privacy. The topics include: Non-interactive private decision tree evaluation; privacy-preserving anomaly detection using synthetic data; local differentially private matrix factorization with mog for recommendations; designing a decision-support visualization for live digital forensic investigations; predictive analytics to prevent voice over ip international revenue sharing fraud; PUA detection based on bundle installer characteristics; ML-supported identification and prioritization of threats in the ovvl threat modelling tool; enhancing the performance of spatial queries on encrypted data through graph embedding; crowdsourcing under data poisoning attacks: A comparative study; self-enhancing gps-based authentication using corresponding address; managing secure inter-slice communication in 5g network slice chains; GOOSE: A secure framework for graph outsourcing and sparql evaluation; SGX-ir: Secure information retrieval with trusted processors; readability of privacy policies; proactively extracting iot device capabilities: An application to smart homes; security enumerations for cyber-physical systems; inference-proof monotonic query evaluation and view generation reconsidered; network functions virtualization access control as a service; effective access control in shared-operator multi-tenant data stream management systems; information flow security certification for spark programs. © 2020 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
