AD  - Nirma University, Department of CSE, Ahmedabad, India
AB  - The cloud computing technology is raPIDly increasing day by day as it provides hardware, storage, network as well as platforms and software. There is a risk of various attacks like data breaches, data loss, denial of service etc which creates various kind of security issues. Multiple tenants store their private and confidential data in the cloud. So, cloud security is playing an important role in it. RoT is a very new and useful perspective to accomplish security in the cloud. By applying RoT in the cloud, new trust layer can be generating for the users so that users can deploy their sensitive information without hesitation. In this research, the main objective is to work on achieving RoT. RoT defined with parameters as authentication, identification, privacy, confidentiality, integrity, access control, authorization. The target is to deploy RoT in the cloud using three parameters that are authentication, access control, and confidentiality. For that three proposed models are characterize in this paper. Thus, intruders can't access the cloud data and security can be achieved. © 2020 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
