AD  - The NorthCap University, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Gurugram, India
AB  - Cloud computing is an emerging field in the Information Technology sector which allows users to access resources from cloud servers irrespective of its geographical location. It utilizes the concept of virtualization, service-oriented architecture and parallel computing. It is an on-demand service which is cost-effective, resilient, efficient, and explandable. Since data is generating in big numbers from various fields of life, we require a more innovative way to manage and secure that data. With the growing social platforms, managing Big Data calls for the need for cloud computing. Nowadays access control and security are recent major research problem in cloud computing. Access control is a paradigm by which a specific consumer access resources from cloud server. This paper proposes a novel access control methodology to cope up with the above issues. The model is based on an integrated DNA morse code pattern that provides data security against collision, man-in-the-middle, and internal attacks. It also compares the proposed model with existing approaches. © 2020 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
