AB  - The proceedings contain 28 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Foundations and Practice of Security. The topics include: Lempel-Ziv Compression with Randomized Input-Output for Anti-compression Side-Channel Attacks Under HTTPS/TLS; interpreting Machine Learning Malware Detectors Which Leverage N-gram Analysis; semantic Representation Based on Deep Learning for Spam Detection; using Machine Learning to Detect Anomalies in Embedded Networks in Heavy Vehicles; lightweight IoT Mutual Authentication Scheme Based on Transient Identities and Transactions History; A Rejection-Based Approach for Detecting SQL Injection Vulnerabilities in Web Applications; detecting Ransomware in Encrypted Web Traffic; digital Forensics in Vessel Transportation Systems; Towards Secure TMIS Protocols; Get-your-ID: Decentralized Proof of Identity; ransomware Network Traffic Analysis for Pre-encryption Alert; dynamic Searchable Encryption with Access Control; security Analysis of Auctionity: A Blockchain Based E-Auction; an Efficient Identification Scheme Based on Rank Metric; incorporating Off-Line Attribute Delegation into Hierarchical Group and Attribute-Based Access Control; On Attribute Retrieval in ABAC; command Dependencies in Heuristic Safety Analysis of Access Control Models; protecting Android Apps from Repackaging Using Native Code; TATIS: Trustworthy APIs for Threat Intelligence Sharing with UMA and CP-ABE; Enroll, and Authentication Will Follow: eID-Based Enrollment for a Customized, Secure, and Frictionless Authentication Experience; PAC: Privacy-Preserving Arrhythmia Classification with Neural Networks; Selection and Performance Analysis of CICIDS2017 Features Importance; towards Privacy-Aware Smart Surveillance; a Privacy Protection Layer for Wearable Devices; labelled Network Capture Generation for Anomaly Detection; Validating the DFA Attack Resistance of AES (Short Paper). © 2020 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
