AB  - In this paper, we are going to focus a cloud-based internet of things (IOT) platform-specific model in healthcare sector. Health care sector in remote area is highly dispersed and the citizens are not quite competent enough to avail all the benefit provided by Government to them considering this issue here we have integrated all vital service need for making the model further implementation. The data storage of this cloud-based model can implement azure service for its service delivery to end-user. Healthcare industry generates a massive amount of data to perform and process the services of the citizen. Subsequently, it puts pressure on internet infrastructure so the revolutionary solution emerges to minimize the pressure by using IoT-based cloud infrastructure. It is a structure in which the traditional infrastructure of healthcare industry metamorphoses into IoT-Cloud infrastructure. It is further providing scalability in the delivery of healthcare services. It migrates load to distributed cloud data store via a dedicated link. Both cloud computing and IoT enables as a better collaboration for every industry. The proposed model in this paper allow user to have on-demand access to cloud service. IoT captures citizen detail through sensor. This is an innovative approach that is modifying the interaction value chain between citizen, hospital, and doctor. IoT-cloud ecosystem is a dynamic fine-grained access control scheme © 2020 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
