AB  - The proceedings contain 50 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Web Information Systems Engineering. The topics include: Personalized Book Recommendation Based on a Deep Learning Model and Metadata; DINRec: Deep Interest Network Based API Recommendation Approach for Mashup Creation; co-purchaser Recommendation Based on Network Embedding; community-Based Recommendations on Twitter: Avoiding the Filter Bubble; memory-Augmented Attention Network for Sequential Recommendation; multi-head Attentive Social Recommendation; CPL: A Combined Framework of Pointwise Prediction and Learning to Rank for top-N Recommendations with Implicit Feedback; RTIM: A Real-Time Influence Maximization Strategy; LSCMiner: Efficient Low Support Closed Itemsets Mining; detecting Fraudulent Accounts on Blockchain: A Supervised Approach; pattern Filtering Attention for Distant Supervised Relation Extraction via Online Clustering; adaptive Rule Adaptation in Unstructured and Dynamic Environments; shadowed Authorization Policies - A Disaster Waiting to Happen?; a Dynamic Decision-Making Method Based on Ensemble Methods for Complex Unbalanced Data; collaborative Wireframing for Model-Driven Web Engineering; handling Disagreement in Ontologies-Based Reasoning via Argumentation; a Cost-Efficient Multi-cloud Orchestrator for Benchmarking Containerized Web-Applications; highlighting Weasel Sentences for Promoting Critical Information Seeking on the Web; generating an Evolving Skills Network from Job Adverts for High-Demand Skillset Discovery; picture News Collection: A Dataset for Automatic Picture News Thumbnail Selection; locking Mechanism for Concurrency Conflicts on Hyperledger Fabric; a Graph-Based Approach to Explore Relationship Between Hashtags and Images; RDF Graph Anonymization Robust to Data Linkage; WebEL: Improving Entity Linking with Extra Web Contexts; entity Disambiguation Based on Parse Tree Neighbours on Graph Attention Network; bibliographic Name Disambiguation with