AB  - The proceedings contain 238 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Information Systems and Technologies. The topics include: Access control for social care platforms using fast healthcare interoperability resources; a framework to develop gamified health applications to aid the treatment of non-communicable diseases; impact of parameter tuning on machine learning based breast cancer classification; interactive support system using humanoid robot for rehabilitation of gross motricity in children; online peer support groups to combat digital addiction: User acceptance and rejection factors; automated computer-aided design of cranial implants using a deep volumetric convolutional denoising autoencoder; computational system for heart rate variability analysis; principles for design of simulated cases in teaching enterprise modelling; effectiveness and fun metrics in a pervasive game experience: A systematic literature review; the gamification in the design of computational applications to support the autism treatments: an advance in the state of the art; breast cancer classification with missing data imputation; Using the SPAR ontology network to represent the scientific production of a university: A case study; factors affecting adoption and use of e-learning by business employees in Cameroon; Result of the methodology for learning english distance with the use of TICs. case study: central university of Ecuador; is it all about frequency?: Students’ digital competence and tablet use; using gamification in software engineering teaching: Study case for software design; geolympus - Cloud platform for supporting location-based applications: A pervasive game experience; Bio-inspired petal-shape UWB antenna for indoor applications; single-step approach to phaseless contrast-source inverse scattering. © 2019 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
