AB  - With the development of cloud technology and the continuous evolution of software architecture, micro-service has become a very popular software development architecture mode, which is more suitable for the situation of business expanding and rapid function iteration. This paper discusses the basic concepts and main features of micro-service architecture, and analyzes the shortcomings of the traditional architecture, so as to obtain the basic requirements of access control in micro-service environment. By studying the traditional access control technology, this paper analyzes its limitations and shortcomings in the micro-service environment, and proposes an access control optimization model based on RBAC. © 2019 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
