AD  - Sri Sairam Engineering College, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Chennai, India
AB  - The resources that are associated with cloud are majorly prone to security threats. This is evident from the instance that accounts which are intruded store the data in cloud platforms. Eventually providing a security mechanism to overcome this issue becomes more complex. We use identity-based cryptosystem to focus on the problem of private matching over outsourced encrypted datasets that’s implies the management of certification. To solve this problem, we propose an Identity-Based Private Matching Biometric Features scheme(IBPMBF),that prevents the leakage of personal information using fine-grained authorization that enables the privileged cloud server to perform operations there by securing the private data and Biometric Features for Continuous Authentication. © 2019 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
