AB  - The proceedings contain 46 papers. The topics discussed include: a prior knowledge based approach to improving accuracy of web services clustering; rule-based model for smart building supervision and management; framework for building self-adaptive component applications based on reinforcement learning; a holistic evaluation of Docker containers for interfering microservices; modeling sentiment polarity in support ticket data for predicting cloud service subscription renewal; a system for predicting health of an e-contract; cost efficient scheduling for delay-sensitive tasks in edge computing system; a change tracking framework for financial documents; bazaar-blockchain: a blockchain for bazaar-based cloud markets; a framework for online process concept drift detection from event streams; a fluctuation-aware approach for predictive web service composition; a two-phase method of QoS prediction for situated service recommendation; enabling intelligent business processes with context awareness; patterns for process edification in process-aware information systems; digital asset management with distributed permission over blockchain and attribute-based access control; and achieving a fault tolerant and reliable cloud data center network. © 2018 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
