AD  - Ponnaiyah Ramajayam Institute of Science & Technology, Thanjavur, India
AB  - A sight saver cloud is designed with a view that the operating drivers on road will have periodical eye check up and continually monitored review and follow up process, with the help of latest computing and communication technology. The defects in the eye can be captured using an imaging device, say the high resolution camera incorporated with the present day smart phones or tabs or even using a portable ocular measurement device. This first input will be fed into a centralized cloud and the qualified ophthalmologists will diagnose the image at his or her location. Then the cloud administrator receives the diagnostic information fed by the ophthalmologists which will aid in treating the drivers who have defects in their eye sight. The driver will be delivered with an sms to approach the nearest point of contact for medication or goggles so as to have a safer driving experience, by the cloud administrator. This process will have a periodical and continual follow up as the data is stored in a cloud. While porting data to and fro of the cloud, authentication and authorization process is also carried out with bio metric characteristics of the cloud user. © 2018 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
