AB  - With the development of cloud computing, more and more enterprises will outsource their sensitive data for sharing in a cloud. However most existing works follow the model of 'one size fits all' over encrypted outsourced cloud data, and ignore personalized search intention. Therefore, it is important to, design a searchable encryption scheme that supports personalized search and fine-grained access control. In this paper, for the first time, we build a user interest model for an individual user according to the department the user belongs to and his search history. To address the limitations of the model of 'one size fits all' and access control, we propose attribute-based encryption with personalized search (AEPS) which is suitable to multi-user sharing cloud computing search services. © 2018 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
