AB  - --The boom of cloud computing, increases the security and privacy of data plays a major role in data transfer, outsourcing of data, data storage. Outsourcing of data in the untrusted cloud servers are to be monitored or managed keenly for security and privacy issues. Unauthorized access of data is a most challenging issue in cloud environment. Access control mechanisms plays a major role in securing the data in cloud. In cloud computing, Attribute Based Encryption provides both security as well as data access control. This paper presents the analysis of different access control mechanisms used in cloud for data security. The shortcomings of different access methods are addressed. The ABAC mechanism is applied in cloud environment. Earlier access control techniques are applied only for centralized environment and also it doesn’t provide fine grained data access control. © 2019 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
