AD  - Khammam Institute of Technology and Sciences, Department of CSE, Khammam, India
AD  - Nagole Institute of Technology and Science, Department of CSE, Hyderabad, India
AB  - The outsourcing process is computationally secure if it is performed without unveiling to the other external agent or cloud, either the original data or the actual solution to the computations. Secure multiparty computation computes a certain function without revealing their private secret information. In this paper, we presented a new secure and computationally efficient protocol utilizing multi cloud servers view. In our proposed protocol, encrypted data by different users is transformed to cloud. The protocol being non-interactive between users, gives the comparatively lesser computational and communication complexity. The analysis of our proposed protocol is also presented at the end of the paper. © 2019 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
