AB  - The proceedings contain 36 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Network and System Security. The topics include: Secure semantic search based on two-level index over encrypted cloud; fast QuadTree-based pose estimation for security applications using face biometrics; walking on the cloud: Gait recognition, a wearable solution; EMA-LAB: Efficient multi authorisation level attribute based access control; SCARA: A framework for secure cloud-assisted RFID authentication for smart building access control; continuous authentication on smartphone by means of periocular and virtual keystroke; real-time IoT device activity detection in edge networks; enhanced keystroke recognition based on moving distance of keystrokes through WiFi; Analyzing the communication security between smartphones and IoT based on CORAS; Analysis on the block reward of fork after withholding (FAW); vulnerability assessment for unmanned systems autonomy services architecture; LA3: A lightweight accountable and anonymous authentication scheme for resource-constrained devices; An efficient privacy preserving batch authentication scheme with deterable function for VANETs; privacySearch: An end-user and query generalization tool for privacy enhancement in web search; revisiting website fingerprinting attacks in real-world scenarios: A case study of shadowsocks; User relationship classification of facebook messenger mobile data using WEKA; using software visualization for supporting the teaching of MapReduce; DBAF: Dynamic binary analysis framework and its applications; context-aware failure-oblivious computing as a means of preventing buffer overflows; ATPG binning and SAT-based approach to hardware trojan detection for safety-critical systems; Adding confidential transactions to cryptocurrency IOTA with bulletproofs; android malware detection methods based on the combination of clustering and classification. © 2018 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
