AB  - Since the concept of "Cloud Computing" was first put forward in 2006, cloud computing has become a very popular research direction in the IT field in recent years. It enables users to access computing, storage, network and other resources from a shared, configurable resource pool through network convenience and on-demand. The cloud computing data center can provide more efficient and personalized elastic computing resource allocation ability, and can more effectively use the existing IT equipment resources in Colleges and universities to create a cloud platform that is more in line with the needs of scientific research in Colleges and universities. The cloud computing data center can provide more efficient and personalized elastic computing resource allocation ability, and can make more effective use of the existing IT equipment resources in the enterprise, and create a cloud platform that is more in line with the needs of the enterprise. Openstack is one of the most active projects in the current open source cloud computing technology community. Many vendors have joined this open source project, such as HP, Redhat, IBM and so on. To Openstack the support of the hardware server architecture level, many storage service vendors have also launched their own storage drive for OpenStack. This largely promoted the development of Openstack's open source project. At the same time, because the project itself is open source, the use of the software is almost no cost, does not involve business use authorization, and the underlying source code users can be controlled. In the familiar code structure technology, the program developers can develop two times for their specific needs. In order to solve these problems, this paper uses the open source resource management platform OpenStack to build the private cloud infrastructure of the school, and finally realizes the construction of the private cloud computing platform of the campus network. © 2019 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
