AD  - MLR Institute of Technology, Hyderabad, India
AD  - MLR Institute of Technology, Computer Science & Engineering, Hyderabad, India
AB  - Controlling the information in open distributed system is a critical issue. Data access control and distribution is one of the testing issues in open cloud storage system. Cloud storage provides many benefits, on the one side it support the data owner in technical aspects and management, and support data owner to distribute the resources to excepted users. Other side, it accompanies new threats to privacy and security. CP-ABE is generally embraced as a useful strategy to give versatile, close grained and strong data connection control for cloud storage with sincere but intrigued cloud servers. In the present CP-ABE method single authority is responsible for the consumer’s permissibility validation and secret key generation, so it is a time consuming task. In large cloud storage, the single attribute authority take care the entire cloud storage and permissibility validation becomes a time consuming task. This causes the users to wait for a long time in order to get their secret keys, thereby makes the system less efficient. Multiple authority access control schemes are put forward to eradicate all the problems faced by single authority but still it lacks behind the performance bottleneck and low efficiency. The problem is with the management of disjoint set by each authority in a multiple authority system. In this paper we put forward a unique diverse structure to eradicate the execution bottleneck and to implement a more methodical access control method with a suitable scrutinizing mechanism. In our structure user permissibility validation is distributed to multiple authorities, which means the multiple authorities manage a universal set of attributes rather than disjoint sets. At the same time we introduce central authority which is accountable for dispensation of secret keys. To give extra shot of security we incorporate scrutinizing the activity of attribute authorities, which will detect any malicious activity by the attribute authority. Another aspect of the paper is embedding Timed Release Encryption in CPABE. Time stamp is allocated with each of the files uploaded in the cloud storage. Thus enhance the security of the data. © 2018 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
