AB  - A new 3 factor authentication access control system is proposed for cloud based web applications. Traditional authentication involves a username and password along with a onetime password on a mobile or email device. We propose a secure layer of authentication where a user holds a secret key in a secure device issued by the issuing central authority. This portable device with key is used as the secure 3rd authentication step. This is greatly useful when users use shared computers i.e, same computer used by multiple users. We also identify and notify if the key has been manipulated and used by a hacker to gain another user’s access by implementing an alert mechanism and also to lock the user by making the issued keys invalid. © 2018 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
