AB  - The proceedings contain 23 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Emerging Technologies for Developing Countries. The topics include: E-Healthcare Knowledge Creation Platform Using Action Research; framework for Dynamic Web Services Composition Guided by Live Testing; modernization of Legacy Software Tests to Model-Driven Testing; porting the Pay with a (Group) Selfie (PGS) Payment System to Crypto Currency; cloud Digital Forensics Evaluation and Crimes Detection; detecting Malware Domains: A Cyber-Threat Alarm System; intrusion Detection Using Unsupervised Approach; cloud Computing and Virtualization in Developing Countries; mixed Method: An Aggregated Method for Handover Decision in Heterogeneous Wireless Networks; analysis and Effect of Feature Selection Over Smartphone-Based Dataset for Human Activity Recognition; empowering Graduates for Knowledge Economies in Developing Countries; designing an Electronic Health Security System Framework for Authentication with Wi-Fi, Smartphone and 3D Face Recognition Technology; investigating TOE Factors Affecting the Adoption of a Cloud-Based EMR System in the Free-State, South Africa; analysis of the Impact of Cognitive Vehicular Network Environment on Spectrum Sensing; high Availability of Charging and Billing in Vehicular Ad Hoc Network; developing the IoT to Support the Health Sector: A Case Study from Kikwit, DRÂ Congo; designing a Framework for Smart IoT Adaptations; aBAC Based Online Collaborations in the Cloud; evaluating Query Energy Consumption in Document Stores; joint Energy Demand Prediction and Control. © 2017 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.
